    verified("summon.trigger_is_a_membership_list", "summon_event_dispatch",
             "*** 'WHEN THIS CARD IS SUMMONED' IS A DATA TABLE, NOT A PREDICATE IN THE cls RECORD. "
             "0x02265768(r0 = event code) is the summon-trigger evaluator; it runs after every "
             "summon with r4 = the global summon record 0x02298A28 ({+0x02 side, +0x04 zone, "
             "+0x0E cid, +0x10 flags, +0x12 a second cid}) and returns early unless the summoned "
             "card's zone is face-up. THREE CALLERS, THREE CODES: 0x02267A38 passes 7 (NORMAL "
             "summon), 0x02268B7C passes 8 (FLIP summon), 0x0226878A passes 9 (SPECIAL summon). It "
             "computes ONE flag r5 and, when it is non-zero, posts the event at 0x02265CA8 via the "
             "register-prim 0x021D3168 with zone -> bits 16..20, side -> bit 31, the event code -> "
             "bits 25..30 and -- decisively -- `movs r6,#2 ; lsls r6,r6,#0x14` = 0x00200000, i.e. "
             "THE SELECTOR IS HARD-CODED TO 1. So a summon trigger can only ever be dispatched to "
             "a cls1 record; cls3 is unreachable from it. And 0x0224A115 -- the `+0C` value shared "
             "by three of the five native 'when this card is Synchro Summoned' cards, and the "
             "obvious-looking candidate for a was-I-just-summoned test -- is 0x0224A114|1 = "
             "`movs r0,#2 ; bx lr`, the ubiquitous slot3 always-activatable stub "
             "(dispatch.cls_slot_roles). It says nothing about the summon. "
             "r5 COMES FROM NINE SORTED cid LISTS searched with the generic binary search "
             "0x02022E14(value, table, count), plus one per-cid switch of special conditions: "
             "0x0228F7AC x0x67 (code 7), 0x0228F5B8 x0x12 (code 7 + tribute, the Monarchs), "
             "0x0228F580 x0x0C (code 8), 0x0228F63A x0x1F (code 9, NO further gate = plain 'when "
             "this card is Special Summoned'), 0x0228F5DC x0x17 (code 9 + [+0x12] == cid), "
             "0x0228F6C0 x0x24 (code 9 + [0x02298A28+0x10] & 1), 0x0228F598 x0x10 (code 7 or 8), "
             "0x0228F60A x0x18 (code 7 or 9), 0x0228F678 x0x23 (any code). 0x0228F6C0 is the "
             "'when Synchro / Fusion / Ritual Summoned' set -- it holds Mist Wurm 0x1D7D, "
             "Locomotion R-Genex 0x2045, Trishula 0x221C, Vylon Alpha 0x24B1, Junk Warrior, Black "
             "Rose Dragon, Formula Synchron, Karakuri Burei, the Vylons, the 'when Fusion "
             "Summoned' HEROes and two Rituals -- so [0x02298A28+0x10] bit 0 means 'this Special "
             "Summon was a PROPER summon via a summoning procedure'. "
             "HOW TO USE IT: adding a cid to the right list plus a cls1 record gives a donor a "
             "native summon trigger; hooking one of the `bl 0x02022E14` call sites instead gives "
             "arbitrary code on that summon with the cid live, and returning the engine's own "
             "verdict leaves the dispatch byte-identical (card.azure_eyes_silver_dragon PART G). "
             "*** IN-GAME CONFIRMED 2026-08-24: a stub hooked at the 0x022658B8 search ran on a "
             "live Synchro Summon, so this evaluator is genuinely the post-summon path. "
             "*** AND THE LIST-INSERT HALF IS NOW IN-GAME CONFIRMED TOO (2026-08-30, "
             "card.ninja_grandmaster_hanzo_clause1, first test): a RECORDS-FREE donor "
             "(Melchid 0x13E7) inserted into the code-7 list 0x0228F7AC over the phantom 0x14CC, "
             "plus one cls1 row, fired its Normal-Summon trigger. *** SECOND INDEPENDENT IN-GAME "
             "CONFIRMATION (in-game confirmed by user 2026-09-08, first test, all five oracles): "
             "card.boggart_knight was RE-HOMED off Vampire Orchis 0x15D4 -- a real Effect Monster "
             "borrowed only for her native cls1 record -- onto the records-free vanilla Molten "
             "Behemoth 0x13A5, using THREE rows: code-7 list over the phantom 0x0E74, cls1 record "
             "over 0x0E11 (Boggart 0x2346's cls1[1227] verbatim, which is byte-identical to "
             "Orchis's cls1[278] apart from the cid), criteria row over 0x0E20 (Boggart's own row "
             "1235 {0x0048, 0x0223CA71, 0x00900002}). It also proves the recipe COMPOSES: the same "
             "donor simultaneously carries an ARM9 set-code insert and an ov5 predicate stub, and "
             "a later chain step (tg_rush_rhino) deleting the 0x2346 TEMPLATE rows does not "
             "regress it, because the donor owns its own rows and the engine binary-searches by "
             "cid, never by row index. PREFER THIS OVER THE HOOK. It is "
             "ONE u16 in a sorted list plus ONE cls1 row and ZERO code -- no ov5 cave slot, so the "
             "card stays puzzle-safe -- whereas the hook costs a stub and makes the card "
             "normal-duel-only. The hook is for donors that ALREADY own a cls1 record (which is "
             "the only reason card.azure_eyes_silver_dragon needed it: a second dispatchable cls1 "
             "record is Spirit-only, see dispatch.second_cls1_record_is_spirit_only), or when the "
             "trigger needs a condition no list expresses. EVERY list has droppable phantoms for a "
             "count-neutral insert except 0x0228F6C0 (code 9 + proper summon), measured "
             "2026-08-30: c7 0x0228F7AC has nine (0xE74, 0xE7E, 0xE7F, 0x14CC, 0x15D0, 0x19C0, "
             "0x19D3, 0x1B1A, 0x2346), c8 0x0228F580 has exactly ONE (0x1A9F), c9 0x0228F63A has "
             "five (0xE12, 0x167C, 0x176C, 0x1ABE, 0x1ABF), and the 'any code' list 0x0228F678 has "
             "six. ⚠️ c8's single phantom is the scarcest slot in the whole subsystem -- spend it "
             "deliberately.",
             "import struct\n"
             "img = env.image('ov3'); base = env.base('ov3')\n"
             "# the three callers and their event-code immediates\n"
             "for site, code in ((0x02267A38, 7), (0x0226878A, 9), (0x02268B7C, 8)):\n"
             "    assert h.bl_target(site, 'ov3') == 0x02265768, f'{site:#x} no longer calls the evaluator'\n"
             "    assert h.u16(site - 6, 'ov3') == 0x2000 | code, f'{site:#x} event-code immediate drifted'\n"
             "# the evaluator's prologue: the summon record and the incoming code\n"
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x02265768, 8, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('f8b588b09b4c061c'), 'evaluator prologue drifted'\n"
             "# the posted event word forces SELECTOR 1 (bit 21) -- movs r6,#2 ; lsls r6,r6,#0x14\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x02265C8E, 'ov3') == 0x2602, 'movs r6,#2 drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x02265C94, 'ov3') == 0x0536, 'lsls r6,r6,#0x14 drifted'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x02265CA8, 'ov3') == 0x021D3168, 'the event post moved'\n"
             "assert (2 << 0x14) == 0x00200000 and ((0x00200000 >> 21) & 7) == 1, 'selector arithmetic'\n"
             "# the nine lists: (bl site, count-immediate site, table-LDR site, table, count).\n"
             "# 0x022658B8 is the odd one -- an `ldrh r7,[r4,#0x12]` sits between the count and the bl.\n"
             "LISTS = ((0x022657A2, 0x022657A0, 0x0226579E, 0x0228F7AC, 0x67),\n"
             "         (0x022657B8, 0x022657B6, 0x022657B4, 0x0228F5B8, 0x12),\n"
             "         (0x02265878, 0x02265876, 0x02265874, 0x0228F580, 0x0C),\n"
             "         (0x022658B8, 0x022658B4, 0x022658B2, 0x0228F63A, 0x1F),\n"
             "         (0x022658E2, 0x022658E0, 0x022658DE, 0x0228F5DC, 0x17),\n"
             "         (0x022658FC, 0x022658FA, 0x022658F8, 0x0228F6C0, 0x24),\n"
             "         (0x02265C28, 0x02265C26, 0x02265C24, 0x0228F598, 0x10),\n"
             "         (0x02265C40, 0x02265C3E, 0x02265C3C, 0x0228F60A, 0x18),\n"
             "         (0x02265C50, 0x02265C4E, 0x02265C4C, 0x0228F678, 0x23))\n"
             "for site, cnt_site, ldr_site, tbl, cnt in LISTS:\n"
             "    assert h.bl_target(site, 'ov3') == 0x02022E14, f'{site:#x} is not the list search'\n"
             "    assert h.u16(cnt_site, 'ov3') == 0x2200 | cnt, f'{site:#x} count immediate drifted'\n"
             "    w = h.u16(ldr_site, 'ov3')\n"
             "    assert w & 0xF800 == 0x4800, f'{site:#x} table load is not an LDR literal'\n"
             "    got = h.u32(((ldr_site + 4) & ~3) + (w & 0xFF) * 4, 'ov3')\n"
             "    assert got == tbl, f'{site:#x} table is {got:#x}, expected {tbl:#x}'\n"
             "    rows = struct.unpack_from(f'<{cnt}H', img, tbl - base)\n"
             "    assert all(rows[i] < rows[i + 1] for i in range(cnt - 1)), f'{tbl:#x} not strictly sorted'\n"
             "# the four native 'when this card is Synchro Summoned' cards are in the PROPER list\n"
             "proper = struct.unpack_from('<36H', img, 0x0228F6C0 - base)\n"
             "cls1 = {h.u32(0x022860D4 + i * 24, 'ov3') & 0xFFFF for i in range(0x535)}\n"
             "for cid in (0x1D7D, 0x2045, 0x221C, 0x24B1):\n"
             "    assert cid in proper, f'{cid:#06x} left the proper-summon trigger list'\n"
             "    assert cid in cls1, f'{cid:#06x} lost its cls1 record'\n"
             "# 0x0224A115 is the always-activatable stub, NOT a summon test\n"
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x0224A114, 4, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('02207047'), '0x0224A114 is not movs r0,#2 ; bx lr'\n"
             "# the count-neutral insert budget: how many phantoms each list still has.\n"
             "# c8 having exactly ONE is the scarcity the claim warns about.\n"
             "import json\n"
             "names = json.load(open('scratch/cid_to_name.json', encoding='utf-8'))\n"
             "PHANTOMS = {0x0228F7AC: 9, 0x0228F5B8: 3, 0x0228F580: 1, 0x0228F63A: 5,\n"
             "            0x0228F5DC: 2, 0x0228F6C0: 0, 0x0228F598: 4, 0x0228F60A: 4,\n"
             "            0x0228F678: 6}\n"
             "for _site, _cs, _ls, tbl, cnt in LISTS:\n"
             "    rows = struct.unpack_from(f'<{cnt}H', img, tbl - base)\n"
             "    free = sum(1 for c in rows if str(c) not in names)\n"
             "    assert free == PHANTOMS[tbl], \\\n"
             "        f'{tbl:#x} has {free} phantoms, expected {PHANTOMS[tbl]} -- insert budget changed'\n"
             "assert PHANTOMS[0x0228F580] == 1, 'the c8 scarcity warning is stale'\n"
             "# card.ninja_grandmaster_hanzo_clause1 spent c7's 0x14CC; it is still a phantom here\n"
             "# because the committed oracle is the STOCK image, which no patch modifies.\n"
             "assert str(0x14CC) not in names, '0x14CC is a real card -- the c7 insert is unsound'\n",
             ["notes/azure-eyes-clause2-findings.md",
              "notes/ninja-grandmaster-hanzo-findings.md"], addr=0x02265768, oracle="ov3")

    verified("rider.node_writer_and_kind_byte", "continuous_riders",
             "*** THE RIDER NODE WRITER, AND THE DURATION NIBBLE HIDING IN ITS KIND ARGUMENT. "
             "0x0219F190(r0 = side, r1 = slot, r2 = kind BYTE, r3 = key, [caller sp+0] = param) "
             "allocates a node index via 0x0219F020 (first free of 0x100; pool 0x0229D33C, stride "
             "10), appends it to the ZONE chain whose head is 0x0229AC94 + side*0xB3C + 0x3E + "
             "slot*0x14 (== 0x0229ACD2 + ...) by walking next-links at 0x0229D344, and fills the "
             "node: [+0] = key, [+2] low nibble = kind & 0xF, [+2] bits 4..7 = (kind & 0xF0) >> 4, "
             "[+4] = param, [+6] = [0x0229DD14+0x2C], [+8] = 0 (next). It returns -1 without "
             "writing when the pool is full. *** THE HIGH NIBBLE OF THE KIND BYTE IS A PER-TURN "
             "COUNTDOWN, not part of the kind -- see rider.turn_sweeper. A caller passing kind = "
             "0x12 therefore creates a kind-2 (family 1, so rider.two_walker_families' "
             "0x021A1430 sees it) node that survives exactly one turn boundary. "
             "THE QUEUED ROUTE to the same writer is 0x021C479C(side, slot, key, kind byte, "
             "[caller sp+0] = param), which packs animation command 0x35 | (side ? 0x8000 : 0) "
             "with arg1 = slot | kind<<8, arg2 = key, arg3 = param; its handler 0x021C3E68 -> "
             "0x021BE044 unpacks it (side from bit 0x8000; arg2's own bit 0x8000 selects the "
             "OTHER chain writer 0x0219F230) and calls 0x0219F190 with the FULL kind byte intact. "
             "Both routes are legal from ordinary effect code: the summon-trigger evaluator "
             "0x02265768 itself calls 0x021C479C at 0x02265C6C.",
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x0219F190, 4, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('f8b5051c'), 'node writer prologue drifted'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x0219F19A, 'ov3') == 0x0219F020, 'the node allocator call moved'\n"
             "# the field stores, in order: kind nibbles into [+2], key, param, turn stamp, next\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0219F1F2, 'ov3') == 0x804A, 'strh r2,[r1,#2] (kind) drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0219F208, 'ov3') == 0x804A, 'strh r2,[r1,#2] (duration) drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0219F20C, 'ov3') == 0x800F, 'strh r7,[r1] (key) drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0219F20E, 'ov3') == 0x808A, 'strh r2,[r1,#4] (param) drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0219F214, 'ov3') == 0x80CA, 'strh r2,[r1,#6] (turn stamp) drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0219F218, 'ov3') == 0x810A, 'strh r2,[r1,#8] (next) drifted'\n"
             "# the high-nibble extraction: (kind & 0xF0) >> 4 into bits 4..7\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0219F1FA, 'ov3') == 0x23F0, 'movs r3,#0xf0 drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0219F1FC, 'ov3') == 0x4023, 'ands r3,r4 drifted'\n"
             "# the queued route reaches the same writer with the kind byte intact\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021C47AA, 'ov3') == 0x2035, 'command opcode 0x35 drifted'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021C47C6, 'ov3') == 0x021C3BC8, '0x021C479C no longer queues'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021BE08A, 'ov3') == 0x0219F190, 'the 0x35 handler no longer calls the writer'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021BE07E, 'ov3') == 0x0219F230, 'the 0x35 handler alternate writer moved'\n"
             "# and the engine itself makes that call from the summon-trigger evaluator\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x02265C6C, 'ov3') == 0x021C479C, 'the native attach in 0x02265768 moved'\n",
             ["notes/azure-eyes-clause2-findings.md", "otn-attached-effect-rider"],
             addr=0x0219F190, oracle="ov3")

    verified("rider.turn_sweeper", "continuous_riders",
             "*** HOW A RIDER EXPIRES, AND HOW TO SPELL 'UNTIL THE END OF THE NEXT TURN'. "
             "0x0219F9E0 sweeps every node index 1..0xFF and dispatches on the node's kind nibble "
             "through a halfword jump table at 0x0219FA2C (add-pc base 0x0219FA2E): kinds 0/4/5 -> "
             "0x0219FAEE = keep forever; kinds 1/2 -> 0x0219FA3E = `n = [node+2]>>4 ; if n == 0 "
             "free the node else n -= 1` -- UNCONDITIONAL, it never looks at the key; kind 3 -> "
             "0x0219FA5C = free only for keys 0x18D9 / 0x1F6A; kinds 6/7/8 -> 0x0219FA6C = family "
             "2, which resolves the node's SOURCE LOCATOR to a cid via 0x021A36EC and then runs a "
             "per-cid switch whose 0x175D arm (Weapon Change, printed 'until the End Phase of your "
             "opponent's NEXT turn') at 0x0219FACE frees the node when [0x0229DD14+0x40] > "
             "[node+4]. *** IT RUNS EXACTLY ONCE PER TURN: its only caller is 0x021C1358 inside "
             "0x021C12F0, the handler for animation opcode 3 (arm 0x021C3D3C), which is queued by "
             "the phase-8 handler 0x02258C3C at its step 0; phase 8 is the last entry of the "
             "phase-handler table 0x0226D2B0 driven by 0x0219D4C0 (`ldr r0,[0x0226D2B0 + phase*4] "
             "; blx r0`), and that same handler's next step queues opcode 4 -> 0x021C102C, the "
             "SOLE site that toggles the turn player ([0x0229DD14+0x34] ^= 1) and increments the "
             "TURN COUNTER ([0x0229DD14+0x40] += 1). CONSEQUENCE: a kind-1/2 node created with "
             "duration nibble 1 (kind byte 0x1N) survives the sweep at the end of the turn it was "
             "made in and is freed by the sweep at the end of the following turn -- 'until the end "
             "of the NEXT turn' with no code edit at all; nibble 0 is 'until the end of this "
             "turn'. The family-2 route to the same duration (param = the current turn number, as "
             "0x0221B18A does when it attaches a kind-7 node) is unusable for a NEW card because "
             "its arm is cid-gated on 0x175D.",
             "import struct\n"
             "img = env.image('ov3'); base = env.base('ov3')\n"
             "# the kind jump table, decoded the way the code does it\n"
             "tbl, pcbase = 0x0219FA2C, 0x0219FA2E\n"
             "arms = [pcbase + struct.unpack_from('<h', img, tbl + i * 2 - base)[0] for i in range(9)]\n"
             "assert arms == [0x0219FAEE, 0x0219FA3E, 0x0219FA3E, 0x0219FA5C, 0x0219FAEE,\n"
             "                0x0219FAEE, 0x0219FA6C, 0x0219FA6C, 0x0219FA6C], f'kind arms moved: {[hex(a) for a in arms]}'\n"
             "# the kind-1/2 countdown arm: extract bits 4..7, free at 0, else decrement\n"
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x0219FA3E, 8, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('0106090f08d0491e'), 'the countdown arm drifted'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x0219FAEA, 'ov3') == 0x0219F03C, 'the node-free call moved'\n"
             "# the Weapon Change turn-compare arm\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0219FAD0, 'ov3') == 0x6C01, 'ldr r1,[r0,#0x40] (turn counter) drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0219FAD2, 'ov3') == 0x88A0, 'ldrh r0,[r4,#4] (expiry param) drifted'\n"
             "# the sweeper has exactly one caller, inside the opcode-3 handler\n"
             "def bl_callers(target):\n"
             "    out = []\n"
             "    for a in range(base, base + len(img) - 4, 2):\n"
             "        hw, lw = struct.unpack_from('<HH', img, a - base)\n"
             "        if (hw & 0xF800) == 0xF000 and (lw & 0xF800) == 0xF800:\n"
             "            imm = ((hw & 0x7FF) << 12) | ((lw & 0x7FF) << 1)\n"
             "            if imm & (1 << 22): imm -= (1 << 23)\n"
             "            if a + 4 + imm == target: out.append(a)\n"
             "    return out\n"
             "assert bl_callers(0x0219F9E0) == [0x021C1358], 'the sweeper gained or lost a caller'\n"
             "assert bl_callers(0x021C12F0) == [0x021C3D3C], 'the opcode-3 handler gained a caller'\n"
             "# opcode 3 and 4 really are those two arms of the command dispatcher\n"
             "otbl, obase = 0x021C3C5E, 0x021C3C60\n"
             "arm3 = obase + struct.unpack_from('<H', img, otbl + 3 * 2 - base)[0]\n"
             "arm4 = obase + struct.unpack_from('<H', img, otbl + 4 * 2 - base)[0]\n"
             "assert (arm3, arm4) == (0x021C3D3C, 0x021C3D42), f'command arms moved: {hex(arm3)}, {hex(arm4)}'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(arm4, 'ov3') == 0x021C102C, 'opcode 4 is no longer the turn flip'\n"
             "# the turn flip: toggle [+0x34], then increment [+0x40]\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021C1046, 'ov3') == 0x6B4A, 'ldr r2,[r1,#0x34] drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021C104A, 'ov3') == 0x4042, 'eors r2,r0 drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021C104C, 'ov3') == 0x634A, 'str r2,[r1,#0x34] drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021C104E, 'ov3') == 0x6C0A, 'ldr r2,[r1,#0x40] drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021C1052, 'ov3') == 0x1C52, 'adds r2,r2,#1 drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021C1054, 'ov3') == 0x640A, 'str r2,[r1,#0x40] drifted'\n"
             "# phase 8 is the last handler in the table and it queues opcode 3 at step 0\n"
             "assert h.u32(0x0226D2B0 + 8 * 4, 'ov3') == 0x02258C3D, 'phase 8 handler moved'\n"
             "assert h.u32(0x0226D2B0 + 9 * 4, 'ov3') == 0, 'the phase table is no longer 9 entries'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x02258C68, 'ov3') == 0x021C3BC8, 'the opcode-3 queue call moved'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x02258C5A, 'ov3') == 0x2003, 'the queued opcode is no longer 3'\n",
             ["notes/azure-eyes-clause2-findings.md"], addr=0x0219F9E0, oracle="ov3")

    verified("rider.affect_predicate_protection_link", "continuous_riders",
             "*** WHERE TO GRANT 'CANNOT BE TARGETED **OR DESTROYED** BY CARD EFFECTS', AND WHY "
             "IT IS NOT THE LINK safe_zone USED. 0x021B021C is the general 'may this card "
             "effect affect this monster' predicate: r0 = the acting card's 0x24-byte descriptor, "
             "r1 = the target's side, r2 = its slot, r3 = a TARGETS flag, and the caller's [sp+0] "
             "is the value returned when the monster is PROTECTED. Protected exit 0x021B0296 "
             "(`ldr r0,[sp,#0x58]`), affectable exit 0x021B081E (`movs r0,#1`). At 0x021B058C it "
             "queries Vehicroid Connection Zone's family-1 rider -- `ldr r2,=0x1A5C ; adds r0,r6,#0 "
             "; adds r1,r5,#0 ; bl 0x021A1430 ; cmp r0,#0 ; beq ; b 0x021B0296` -- and that link "
             "sits BEFORE the targets gate, which is read 0x2C bytes later at 0x021B05BE. Heart of "
             "Clear Water's link at 0x021B05CC, which safe_zone PART D borrowed, sits INSIDE "
             "that gate, and THAT is the entire origin of Safe Zone's documented divergence 'a "
             "non-targeting destruction still resolves'. *** A NON-TARGETING DESTRUCTION REALLY "
             "DOES PASS THROUGH 0x021B058C: caller 0x02245B7A calls the wrapper 0x021B0848 with "
             "its targets argument 0 and, only when the predicate says affectable, calls "
             "0x021CF35C -> 0x021CF31C -> 0x021CDD4C(desc, mask, 0x0E, 2) -- destination zone 0x0E "
             "is the Graveyard, i.e. it destroys the monster; and 0x021B0848 passes 0 as the "
             "predicate's [sp+0x58], so 'protected' returns 0 and the destroy is skipped. NEITHER "
             "this link NOR Dreadmaster's at 0x021B05FA applies a controller test, so a grant "
             "inserted here protects from BOTH players -- drop Safe Zone's `r7+2` opponent check "
             "and the 'neither player' half of a clause is free. Chaining it needs NO frame "
             "surgery, unlike Safe Zone's insert: the native `cmp r0,#0 ; beq ; b 0x021B0296` "
             "already turns a non-zero return into the protected exit. Reachability is inherited "
             "from a SHIPPED in-game result -- Safe Zone's 0x021B05CC hook is in-game confirmed "
             "(2026-07-21) and control reaches 0x021B05CC only by first executing 0x021B0592. "
             "*** IN-GAME CONFIRMED 2026-08-24 for the non-targeting half: with a rider on "
             "this link, a Dragon survived Dark Hole and Smashing Ground -- neither of which "
             "targets -- in a live duel (card.azure_eyes_silver_dragon clause 2). So this link "
             "genuinely does NOT inherit safe_zone's 'a non-targeting destruction still "
             "resolves' divergence; that is measured now, not inferred from 0x02245B7A alone.",
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x021B021C, 8, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('f8b590b00e1c1699'), 'the predicate prologue drifted'\n"
             "# the VCZ link: literal 0x1A5C, the family-1 query, and the protected exit\n"
             "w = h.u16(0x021B058C, 'ov3')\n"
             "assert w & 0xF800 == 0x4800, '0x021B058C is not an LDR literal'\n"
             "assert h.u32(((0x021B058C + 4) & ~3) + (w & 0xFF) * 4, 'ov3') == 0x1A5C, 'the VCZ literal moved'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021B0592, 'ov3') == 0x021A1430, '0x021B0592 is not the family-1 query'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021B0596, 'ov3') == 0x2800, 'cmp r0,#0 after the VCZ query drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021B0296, 'ov3') == 0x9816, 'the protected exit no longer loads [sp,#0x58]'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021B0298, 'ov3') & 0xF800 == 0xE000, '0x021B0298 is no longer the branch to the epilogue'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021B081E, 'ov3') == 0x2001, 'the affectable exit is not movs r0,#1'\n"
             "# the targets gate is LATER, so 0x021B0592 is outside it and Safe Zone's link is inside\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021B05BE, 'ov3') == 0x9800, 'the targets-flag load moved'\n"
             "assert 0x021B0592 < 0x021B05BE < 0x021B05CC, 'the ordering assumption broke'\n"
             "# the wrapper passes 0 as the protected return, and one of its callers is a DESTROY\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021B0878, 'ov3') == 0x9100, 'the wrapper no longer passes 0 as [sp+0]'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021B087A, 'ov3') == 0x9101, 'the wrapper no longer passes 0 as [sp+4]'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021B0882, 'ov3') == 0x021B021C, 'the wrapper no longer calls the predicate'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x02245B82, 'ov3') == 0x021B0848, 'the destroy caller moved'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x02245B78, 'ov3') == 0x9001, 'the destroy caller no longer passes targets = 0'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x02245B92, 'ov3') == 0x021CF35C, 'the destroy call moved'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021CF36E, 'ov3') == 0x021CF31C, '0x021CF35C no longer forwards'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021CF34E, 'ov3') == 0x220E, 'the destination zone is no longer 0x0E (the GY)'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021CF352, 'ov3') == 0x021CDD4C, 'the relocation call moved'\n",
             ["notes/azure-eyes-clause2-findings.md", "notes/safe-zone-findings.md"],
             addr=0x021B058C, oracle="ov3")
    verified("dispatch.token_summon_table", S,
             "TOKEN SUMMONING IS TABLE-DRIVEN, not per-card code. Every token-maker shares slot1 "
             "resolver 0x02207A09 (Scapegoat 0x12D2 cls0[152], Ojama Trio 0x166A cls0[455], "
             "Dandylion 0x19FE cls2[203], Fires of Doomsday 0x1D1E cls0[901], Reptilianne Spawn "
             "0x2125 cls0[1107], Doppelwarrior 0x244D cls2[657], and the CUT Zeta Reticulant 0x1A8A "
             "cls2[220]). The resolver's first act is `ldrh r0,[r5]` (the descriptor cid) -> "
             "`bl 0x021A2EE0`, a LINEAR scan of 0x4C (76) 8-byte records based at 0x0226D484 matching "
             "the u16 at +0 and returning the record base. RECORD LAYOUT: {+0 u16 activating cid, "
             "+2 u16 TOKEN cid, +4 u16 count, +6 u16 mode}. MODE = battle position: 1 = Defense "
             "(Scapegoat, Ojama Trio and Dandylion all print 'in Defense Position'), 0 = Attack "
             "(Doppelwarrior, Nightmare Archfiends), 2 = unspecified/player's choice (Sweet Corn). "
             "The per-cid side flip that puts Ojama Trio's tokens on the OPPONENT's field is a leaf "
             "in the resolver's cid switch at 0x02207BAA (movs r0,#1 / subs r0,r0,r4 / str r0,[sp,#0x10]). "
             "The per-token loop ends in 0x0226925C(r0 = target side, r1 = &locator, r2 = 1, "
             "r3 = mode) — the generic Special Summon entry point, which CONTAINS the known SS-commit "
             "hook summon.ss_commit_hook 0x022692E6 at +0x8A. "
             "⚠️ The table ends at 0x0226D6E4 with NO free gap (the battle-attribute cid lists follow "
             "immediately), so any new row must overwrite an existing one. "
             "⚠️ COUNT DOES NOT MEAN CONSECUTIVE CIDS: the `token_cid + counter` addressing at "
             "0x02207D6E is reached only through a per-cid switch at 0x02207D36, so it applies just to "
             "the cards that own several distinct token cids (Scapegoat x4, Ojama Trio x3, Dandylion "
             "x2, Stray Lambs x2). Of the 28 rows with count >= 2 only 6 have token..token+count-1 "
             "sharing one name; the other 22 reuse a single cid N times via the leaf at 0x02207D9E.",
             "base = 0x0226D484\n"
             "# the lookup is a linear scan of exactly 0x4C records, based at the table\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021A2EF6, 'ov3') == 0x2C4C, 'record count immediate (cmp r4,#0x4C) drifted'\n"
             "w = h.u16(0x021A2EE4, 'ov3')\n"
             "assert w & 0xF800 == 0x4800, '0x021A2EE4 is not an LDR literal'\n"
             "assert h.u32(((0x021A2EE4 + 4) & ~3) + (w & 0xFF) * 4, 'ov3') == base, 'token table base drifted'\n"
             "# every row's activating cid and token cid are in card-id range, count sane\n"
             "rows = [tuple(h.u16(base + i * 8 + k, 'ov3') for k in (0, 2, 4, 6)) for i in range(0x4C)]\n"
             "for cid, tok, cnt, mode in rows:\n"
             "    assert 0x0B00 < cid < 0x2600, f'token-table cid {cid:#x} out of range'\n"
             "    assert 0x0B00 < tok < 0x2600, f'token-table token {tok:#x} out of range'\n"
             "    assert cnt <= 4 and mode <= 2, f'token-table count/mode out of range: {cnt}/{mode}'\n"
             "# the known rows still say what the claim says\n"
             "byc = {c: (t, n, m) for c, t, n, m in rows}\n"
             "assert byc[0x12D2] == (0x0F3E, 4, 1), 'Scapegoat row changed'\n"
             "assert byc[0x166A] == (0x0F4B, 3, 1), 'Ojama Trio row changed'\n"
             "assert byc[0x19FE] == (0x0F55, 2, 1), 'Dandylion row changed'\n"
             "assert byc[0x1A8A] == (0x0F5A, 1, 2), 'Zeta Reticulant row changed'\n"
             "assert byc[0x2299] == (0x0F7E, 1, 2), 'Sweet Corn row changed'\n"
             "# the table abuts the next structure -- no headroom\n"
             "assert base + 0x4C * 8 == 0x0226D6E4, 'token table geometry moved'\n"
             "# the resolver really is shared by those cards\n"
             "for tbl, tbase, tcnt, cid in ((0, 0x0227E64C, 0x51A, 0x12D2), (2, 0x02275C04, 0x2B9, 0x19FE),\n"
             "                              (2, 0x02275C04, 0x2B9, 0x1A8A)):\n"
             "    hit = [i for i in range(tcnt) if h.u32(tbase + i * 24, 'ov3') == cid]\n"
             "    assert hit, f'cid {cid:#x} lost its cls{tbl} record'\n"
             "    assert h.u32(tbase + hit[0] * 24 + 4, 'ov3') == 0x02207A09, \\\n"
             "        f'cid {cid:#x} slot1 is no longer the token resolver'\n",
             ["notes/zeta-reticulant-findings.md"], addr=0x0226D484, oracle="ov3")
