             "player+0x34+zone*0x14 and unpacks it into a key, while 0x02234880 (list form: desc, "
             "side, a, b) takes the already-unpacked key in its arguments; both then make the "
             "IDENTICAL call 0x021C750C(side, x, key, desc[+0x10]) and both bump the counter "
             "desc[+0x10] (with desc[+0x12] and the desc[+0x14 + i*2] entry array handled the same "
             "way). So the storage is shared and the resolver cannot tell which recorder produced "
             "an entry. "
             "Mermaid Archer's resolver 0x0220BFFC switches on the phase code [0x0229AAFC+0x70] "
             "(0x7E / 0x7F / 0x80; 0x80 is the act phase), fetches recorded pick i via the shared "
             "accessor 0x02234904(desc, i), and splits the returned halfword as low byte = side, "
             "high byte = key. THE CATCH: at 0x0220C05C..0x0220C06C it then dereferences that "
             "high byte as a MONSTER-ZONE index — ldr r2,[player + 0x34 + idx*0x14] — so a pick "
             "recorded from a LIST zone would index the board array out of range and read the "
             "wrong card. That much is confirmed and is why Sea Lancer E1 needs a resolver detour. "
             "⚠️ RETRACTED SUB-CLAIM (2026-07-21, superseded by dispatch.pick_halfword_layout): "
             "this fact used to call the high byte an 'index' and prescribed a detour calling "
             "0x0219CA28(side, 0x0F, index). BOTH ARE WRONG. The high byte is the 4-bit KEY field, "
             "and for an off-field pick the off-field template stores the ZONE CODE there (0x0F for "
             "banished, from 0x0219C534) — there is no container index anywhere in the descriptor, "
             "so 0x0219CA28 has nothing to index with. The packed card ref is already stored in the "
