    verified("dispatch.turnlog_once_per_turn_pair", S,
             "*** THE ENGINE'S 'YOU CAN ONLY ACTIVATE 1 X PER TURN' IS THE TURN LOG, and it is a "
             "matched POST/QUERY pair that works for ANY donor -- which makes a hard once-per-turn a "
             "two-shim job with no per-cid engine surgery. POST = 0x021D2584(side, cid, kind, 0): a "
             "thin wrapper that sets r1 = 0x0B and tail-calls the attached-node writer 0x021C479C, "
             "which posts EVENT 0x35 with param (kind<<8)|0x0B and the cid as key. QUERY = "
             "0x021A14E8(side, 0x0B, cid, kind) -> nonzero iff that node is already on this turn's "
             "log. kind 1 = card/effect activation. *** IT IS CID-GENERIC: the poster reads the cid "
             "out of the descriptor (`ldrh r1,[r4]` inside the native cost 0x021E8E74), so a donor "
             "does NOT fall into a do-nothing default arm -- contrast card.darkflare_clause2, where "
             "0x021E7245 posts only from a per-cid switch arm and the donor's default posted nothing. "
             "The native model is POT OF DUALITY 0x2321, whose condition 0x02203259 opens with "
             "exactly `ldrb r0,[r5,#2] ; mov r1,#0xB ; ldrh r2,[r5] ; mov r3,#1 ; bl 0x021A14E8` and "
             "whose cls0 +10 cost is the shared poster 0x021E8E75 (also on Pot of Benevolence 0x21E0 "
             "and Spell Power Grasp 0x1FC8; Ritual Foregone 0x1AF4 and Instant Fusion 0x1AF5 reach it "
             "through the wrapper 0x021EA83D). ⚠️ CORRECTION recorded so it does not get re-derived: "
             "0x021D2B88 is NOT the once-per-turn query (it tests desc[+4]==0x25 and desc[+3]<=4), "
             "and 0x021E4D80 is a Spell-activation-legality gate (it probes cid 0x209B in zone 0x0A), "
             "not the OPT. Both sit next to the real mechanism and look like it. See also Shooting "
             "Quasar PART K, which already ships this pair in-game.",
             "# the poster is the 0xB-slot wrapper around the attached-node writer\n"
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x021D2584, 20, 'ov3') == \\\n"
             "    bytes.fromhex('38b50d1c141c00930b212a1c231cf2f703f938bd'), \\\n"
             "    'the turn-log poster 0x021D2584 drifted'\n"
             "# Pot of Duality's condition really opens with the (side, 0xB, cid, 1) query\n"
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x02203264, 14, 'ov3') == \\\n"
             "    bytes.fromhex('a8782a880b21012301249ef73bf9'), \\\n"
             "    \"Pot of Duality's turn-log query drifted\"\n"
             "# and the three Normal Spells that share the generic poster in cls0 +10\n"
             "def cls0_slot10(cid):\n"
             "    hit = [i for i in range(0x51A) if h.u32(0x0227E64C + i * 24, 'ov3') == cid]\n"
             "    assert len(hit) == 1, f'{cid:#06x} cls0 record count changed: {hit}'\n"
             "    return h.u32(0x0227E64C + hit[0] * 24 + 0x10, 'ov3')\n"
             "for cid in (0x2321, 0x21E0, 0x1FC8):\n"
             "    assert cls0_slot10(cid) == 0x021E8E75, \\\n"
             "        f'{cid:#06x} no longer carries the shared once-per-turn cost'\n",
             ["dragon-shrine-findings", "otn-shooting-quasar"], addr=0x021D2584, oracle="ov3")

    verified("carddata.card_type_reader_is_halved", S,
             "*** 0x0202ABF8(cid) RETURNS card_prop's card_type FIELD SHIFTED RIGHT BY ONE, which "
             "reconciles two encodings that look contradictory until you notice the shift. Body: "
             "`push {r3,lr} ; bl 0x0202A084 ; ldr r0,[r0,#4] ; lsls r0,#0x1A ; lsrs r0,#0x1B ; pop` "
             "-- 0x0202A084(cid) returns the card_prop record pointer and [+4] is the word holding "
             "bits 32..63, so the two shifts keep bits 1..5 of card_type. RAW card_prop values "
             "(bits[32:38], decoded across the whole table against ygoprodeck): 1 = Normal Monster "
             "(224 cards), 3 = Effect (1520) + Flip Effect (95), 5/7 = Fusion, 9 = Ritual, 11 = "
             "Ritual Effect, 13 = Toon, 15 = Spirit, 17 = Union, 19 = Gemini, 21 = Token, 27 = Spell "
             "(865), 29 = Trap (715), 31 = Normal Tuner (5), 33 = Tuner (169), 35/37/39 = Synchro. "
             "HALVED, those become 0 = Normal Monster, 1 = Effect, 2/3 = Fusion, 15 = Normal Tuner, "
             "16 = Tuner, 17/18/19 = Synchro -- which is exactly the {17,18,19} Synchro set and the "
             "'Fusion = 2/3' of synchro.card_type_code. So a runtime 'is this a NORMAL MONSTER?' test "
             "is `0x0202ABF8(cid) in (0, 15)` (15 catches Normal Tuners, which are Normal Monsters). "
             "It lives in ARM9, so it is resident in every duel mode including puzzles. "
             "⚠️ card_prop's RACE column is separately unreliable to decode (donor.card_prop_race) but "
             "the card_type field is not affected -- race 1 = Dragon checks out on Blue-Eyes 0x0ED9, "
             "Luster Dragon 0x160C and Divine Dragon Ragnarok 0x1859.",
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x0202ABF8, 14, 'arm9') == \\\n"
             "    bytes.fromhex('08b5fff743fa40688006c00e08bd'), \\\n"
             "    'the card-type reader 0x0202ABF8 drifted'\n"
             "# `lsls #0x1A` then `lsrs #0x1B` == (x >> 1) & 0x1F on the byte-32 field\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0202AC00, 'arm9') == 0x0680, 'the lsls #0x1A drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0202AC02, 'arm9') == 0x0EC0, 'the lsrs #0x1B drifted'\n",
             ["dragon-shrine-findings"], addr=0x0202ABF8, oracle="arm9")

