             "functions call it, covering 665 of the 3107 records, and **30 of them pass the same r2 "
             "literal 0x00000FB6**. The six biggest -- 0x021F01C1 (115 records), 0x021F03B5 (112), "
             "0x021F0419 (62), 0x021F05A9 (62), 0x021F069D (37), 0x021F0221 (27) -- are all 100%-'Once per "
             "turn' families. The numeric collision with Time Wizard's cid 0x0FB6 is a COINCIDENCE; it is "
             "a sentinel in the rider key space, not a card.\n"
             "*** THE READER: 0x021F01C1 is the BARE gate, six instructions and nothing else -- `ldrb "
             "r0,[desc,#2]` (side), `ldrb r1,[desc,#3]` (zone), `ldr r2,=0x0FB6`, `bl 0x021A1430`, then "
             "return 1 when the walker found NOTHING and 0 when it did. It returns 1, not 2, so per "
             "dispatch.cls_slot_roles slot2 would be consulted -- but 28 of its 115 users have slot2 == 0, "
             "so the 'slot3 = 1 with no slot2' pairing is well precedented and needs no predicate.\n"
             "*** THE WRITER: 0x021C479C(side, zone, key, kind, extra) attaches the rider; 24 sites load "
