             "INTERCHANGEABLE. dispatch.criteria_gy_revive_handler names 0x02207529, which is the "
             "**cls0 SPELL/TRAP** resolver (Premature Burial 0x1366, Call of the Haunted 0x137D, "
             "Birthright 0x1B65, Limit Reverse, Graceful Revival, ...) and has NO cls2 member at "
             "all. A MONSTER TRIGGER -- 'when this card is sent to the GY: target 1 X in your GY; "
             "Special Summon that target' -- uses **0x02207191** instead, paired with the same "
             "slot5 off-field picker 0x02235605. ~40 native cls2 records carry that pair: Colossal "
             "Fighter 0x1E12 cls2[357], Lord Poison 0x156D cls2[112], Sun Dragon Inti 0x21CD, Moon "
             "Dragon Quilla 0x21CE, Lightning Tricorn 0x230D, Dragunity Arma Leyvaten 0x2356, "
             "Supersonic Skull Flame 0x204C and the whole /Assault Mode family.\n"
             "Like every shared resolver here its per-cid switch only picks MODES -- r4 = 1 and "
             "r5 = 2 are set up front at 0x02207198/0x0220719A -- and every unmatched compare "
             "falls through to 0x022072DA = `0x02204730(desc, r4, r5)`, the common body. *** So a "
             "records-free donor cid runs it unchanged, exactly as for 0x0220731D and 0x02207529.\n"
             "THE FULL cls2 TEMPLATE for this clause shape is Colossal Fighter cls2[357] = "
             "{+04 0x02207191, +08 0, +0C 0x021F03B5, +10 0x021E51E5, +14 0x02235605}, where +0C "
             "is 'may I Special Summon?' (0x021F0384) AND 'does a legal target exist?' "
             "(0x02234E78 -> 0x02243FE0), and +10 is the 'You can' tag Botanical Girl also carries "
             "(event.optional_trigger_is_record_shape). Colossal Fighter's own criteria handler is "
             "0x0223D6E1, a DIFFERENT revive handler from 0x0223C9D1 -- match the handler to the "
             "card you are copying the WORD from, not to the record you are copying the SLOTS "
             "from. lightpulsar clause 3 uses this template.",
             "# 0x02207191 is a cls2 resolver; 0x02207529 has no cls2 member\n"
             "def slot1_cids(base, cnt, fn):\n"
             "    return {h.u32(base + i * 24, 'ov3') for i in range(cnt)\n"
             "            if h.u32(base + i * 24 + 4, 'ov3') == fn}\n"
             "c2 = slot1_cids(0x02275C04, 0x2B9, 0x02207191)\n"
             "for cid in (0x1E12, 0x156D, 0x21CD, 0x230D, 0x2356):\n"
             "    assert cid in c2, f'{cid:#06x} left the 0x02207191 cls2 revive family'\n"
             "assert not slot1_cids(0x02275C04, 0x2B9, 0x02207529), \\\n"
             "    '0x02207529 now has a cls2 record -- the two-resolver split has changed'\n"
             "# Colossal Fighter's record, slot for slot\n"
             "i = next(i for i in range(0x2B9) if h.u32(0x02275C04 + i * 24, 'ov3') == 0x1E12)\n"
             "rec = [h.u32(0x02275C04 + i * 24 + k, 'ov3') for k in (4, 8, 0xC, 0x10, 0x14)]\n"
             "assert rec == [0x02207191, 0, 0x021F03B5, 0x021E51E5, 0x02235605], \\\n"
             "    f'Colossal Fighter cls2 template drifted: {[hex(x) for x in rec]}'\n"
             "# the mode defaults and the unnamed-cid fall-through to the common body\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x02207198, 'ov3') == 0x2401 and h.u16(0x0220719A, 'ov3') == 0x2502, \\\n"
