             "param IS the row index among that cid's rows. Proven by the Chaos family: Chaos "
             "Sorcerer 0x16C9, Black Luster Soldier - Envoy of the Beginning 0x16CB and Chaos "
             "Emperor Dragon - Envoy of the End 0x16E4 each own EXACTLY TWO adjacent rows, "
             "0x01000002 (attribute LIGHT) and 0x02000002 (attribute DARK), both under handler "
             "0x0223CA11 — while the single-attribute members of the same hand-SS family own "
             "EXACTLY ONE row each: Inferno 0x16C5 FIRE 0x04000002, Fenrir 0x16C6 WATER "
             "0x03000002, Gigantes 0x16C7 EARTH 0x05000002, Silpheed 0x16C8 WIND 0x06000002. "
             "The consumer is the hand-SS tree leaf 0x0225FA46 (see handss.banish_cost_leaf), "
             "which loops param = 0 then 1, writing the pass index to a global at [lit+0x28] "
             "before each 0x02243FE0 call and comparing the found count against 0x0225CF28(cid). "
             "CONSEQUENCE: giving a donor an 'N different cards' summon cost is pure DATA — add "
             "one criteria row per demanded card; no new predicate code.",
             "B, CNT = 0x022713C4, 0x56C\n"
             "rows = [(h.u16(B + i * 12, 'ov3'), h.u32(B + i * 12 + 4, 'ov3'),\n"
             "         h.u32(B + i * 12 + 8, 'ov3')) for i in range(CNT)]\n"
             "def of(cid):\n"
             "    return [(fn, c) for x, fn, c in rows if x == cid]\n"
             "for cid in (0x16C9, 0x16CB, 0x16E4):\n"
