    verified("dispatch.costless_you_can_tag", S,
             "*** THE ENGINE'S GENERIC COSTLESS 'YOU CAN' IS SLOT4 TAG 0x021E51E5, AND ITS BODY IS "
             "0x021E50DC. This closes the 'SEMANTICS NOT YET PROVEN -- which of the two slots carries "
             "optionality' note on event.optionality_is_the_record: it is SLOT4 (+0x10), the "
             "cost / activation-procedure step, and a card pays nothing yet is still asked. "
             "0x021E51E4 is a compiler thunk -- `ldr r3,=0x021E50DD ; ldr r2,=0x021E51E5 ; cmp r3,r2 ; "
             "bne` compares two DIFFERENT constants, so the branch is always taken and it "
             "unconditionally tail-calls 0x021E50DC. The body is a 3-phase machine on "
             "[0x0229AAFC + 0x7C]: phase 0 runs the slot3 activation condition via 0x0224AD94 and "
             "returns -1 to ABORT if it says no, else calls 0x021EE0E0(desc) and -- when that is "
             "nonzero -- sets prompt id 0x107 (0x0219A6F4), names the card (0x0219A798(desc[+0])) and "
             "OPENS THE YES/NO DIALOG (0x0219A818(side ^ desc[+6], 1)) before yielding. It is fully "
             "cid-generic: the cid comes out of the descriptor, so a donor does not fall into a "
             "do-nothing default arm. POPULATION: 352 records carry the thunk 0x021E51E5 and 93 more "
             "the body 0x021E50DD directly, across all four cls tables -- 445 in total, the largest "
             "slot4 family in the engine, ahead of 0x021E5061 (236) and 0x021E5201 (99). "
             "USE: pair it with a slot3 that returns 2 to give ANY donor an optional, costless "
             "triggered effect (card.maiden_clause2 does exactly this).",
             "for site, want in ((0x021E51E6, 0x021E50DD), (0x021E51E8, 0x021E51E5)):\n"
             "    w = h.u16(site, 'ov3')\n"
             "    assert w & 0xF800 == 0x4800, f'{site:#x} is not an LDR literal'\n"
             "    got = h.u32(((site + 4) & ~3) + (w & 0xFF) * 4, 'ov3')\n"
             "    assert got == want, f'{site:#x} literal is {got:#x}, expected {want:#x}'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021E51F2, 'ov3') == 0x021E50DC, 'the thunk no longer tail-calls the body'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021E50FA, 'ov3') == 0x0224AD94, 'phase 0 no longer runs the slot3 condition'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021E5114, 'ov3') == 0x0219A6F4, 'the prompt setter moved'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021E5124, 'ov3') == 0x0219A818, 'the dialog opener moved'\n"
             "w = h.u16(0x021E5112, 'ov3')\n"
             "assert h.u32(((0x021E5112 + 4) & ~3) + (w & 0xFF) * 4, 'ov3') == 0x107, 'prompt id is not 0x107'\n"
             "import collections\n"
             "pop = collections.Counter()\n"
             "for base, cnt in ((0x0227E64C, 0x51A), (0x022860D4, 0x535),\n"
             "                  (0x02275C04, 0x2B9), (0x02279D74, 0x308)):\n"
             "    for i in range(cnt):\n"
             "        pop[h.u32(base + i * 24 + 0x10, 'ov3')] += 1\n"
             "assert pop[0x021E51E5] == 352, f'thunk population is {pop[0x021E51E5]}, expected 352'\n"
             "assert pop[0x021E50DD] == 93, f'body population is {pop[0x021E50DD]}, expected 93'\n"
             "assert max(v for k, v in pop.items() if k) == 352, 'it is no longer the largest slot4 family'\n",
             ["maiden-with-eyes-of-blue-findings", "eclipse-wyvern-findings"],
             addr=0x021E50DC, oracle="ov3")

