    verified("timing.class1_and_class2_differ_only_at_the_gy_offer", S,
             "*** ANSWERS timing.class_semantics' OPEN QUESTION FOR CLASS 1 vs CLASS 2, "
             "STRUCTURALLY AND OFFLINE: THEY ARE BEHAVIOURALLY IDENTICAL EVERYWHERE EXCEPT THE "
             "GY-ACTION OFFER. 0x0224AF7C has exactly FIVE BL call sites in ov3, and the "
             "instruction immediately after each one is the whole of how its class is consumed: "
             "0x021D3A0A `cmp r0,#0 ; beq`, 0x021D3FF6 `cmp r0,#0 ; bne`, 0x021D40A0 "
             "`cmp r0,#0 ; bne` and 0x021F053E `cmp r0,#0 ; beq` are all BOOLEAN -- they ask "
             "only 'is this a classified trigger at all' -- while 0x021EDC76 `cmp r0,#2 ; beq` "
             "is the ONLY site in the game that can tell 1 from 2. That site is inside the "
             "GY-action offer arm of 0x021EDA14, reached only for a descriptor with "
             "desc[+5] == 2 (dispatch.gy_offer_consults_slot3_and_the_timing_class_can_bypass_it), "
             "where class 2 short-circuits to `movs r0,#1` = offer unconditionally. "
             "*** THE CONSEQUENCE, WHICH IS A TRAP THIS PROJECT HAS ALREADY PAID FOR TWICE: "
             "SWAPPING A NON-GY TRIGGER'S +0x10 BETWEEN THE WHEN TAG 0x021E51E5 AND ANY CLASS-1 "
             "TAG (0x021E50DD et al) IS A PROVABLE NO-OP. There is no code that can observe the "
             "difference. So 'convert this WHEN effect into an IF effect by changing the tag' "
             "CANNOT WORK for anything but a GY ignition, and the miss-timing rule is applied "
             "somewhere else entirely -- still unlocated. vylon_element (2026-06-10) is "
             "built entirely on the opposite belief: its docstring tabulates '+10 == 0 -> never "
             "misses timing', which timing.class_semantics had already measured false on "
             "2026-08-17, and its own notes record that the IF tag 'was NOT enough' without "
             "drawing the conclusion. Setting +0x10 = 0 is NOT a no-op -- it flips all four "
             "booleans -- but it flips them toward LESS classification, not toward never-missing, "
             "which is why that build activates and then resolves nothing.",
             "import struct\n"
             "img, base = env.image('ov3'), env.base('ov3')\n"
             "sites = []\n"
             "for off in range(0, len(img) - 4, 2):\n"
             "    hw1, hw2 = struct.unpack_from('<HH', img, off)\n"
             "    if (hw1 & 0xF800) != 0xF000 or (hw2 & 0xF800) not in (0xF800, 0xE800):\n"
             "        continue\n"
             "    o = ((hw1 & 0x7FF) << 12) | ((hw2 & 0x7FF) << 1)\n"
             "    if o & (1 << 22):\n"
             "        o -= (1 << 23)\n"
             "    if (base + off + 4 + o) & 0xFFFFFFFF == 0x0224AF7C:\n"
             "        sites.append(base + off)\n"
             "assert sites == [0x021D3A0A, 0x021D3FF6, 0x021D40A0, 0x021EDC72, 0x021F053E], \\\n"
             "    f'the classifier call-site set changed: {[hex(s) for s in sites]}'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021EDC76, 'ov3') == 0x2802, 'the GY-offer site no longer cmp r0,#2'\n"
             "for s in (0x021D3A0A, 0x021D3FF6, 0x021D40A0, 0x021F053E):\n"
             "    assert h.u16(s + 4, 'ov3') == 0x2800, f'{s:#x} no longer cmp r0,#0'\n",
             ["notes/vylon-element-findings.md", "scratch/vylon_classifier_consumers.py"],
             addr=0x0224AF7C, oracle="ov3")

