    verified("handss.banish_cost_leaf", S,
             "The 'Special Summon this card from your hand by banishing monster(s) from your GY' "
             "family lives in the hand-SS cid tree as a contiguous cluster at 0x0225E88x-0x0225E8DE "
             "with the compare base held in R7 = 0x16C6 (Fenrir), and it splits into exactly TWO "
             "leaves: 0x0225FA36 (single attribute) reached by Inferno 0x16C5 / Fenrir 0x16C6 / "
             "Gigantes 0x16C7 / Silpheed 0x16C8, and 0x0225FA46 (LIGHT + DARK, i.e. TWO different "
             "demanded cards) reached by Chaos Sorcerer 0x16C9, Black Luster Soldier - Envoy of "
             "the Beginning 0x16CB and Chaos Emperor Dragon - Envoy of the End 0x16E4. "
             "0x0225FA46 is generic in the cid: it takes NO cid-specific constant, and instead "
             "runs two identical passes — `strh 0,[g+0x28]` then 0x02243FE0(side, cid, 0), and "
             "`strh 1,[g+0x28]` then 0x02243FE0(side, cid, 1) — each comparing the criteria-registry "
             "hit count against the required count from 0x0225CF28(cid), clearing the r7 result "
             "flag on a shortfall. The per-card data therefore lives ENTIRELY in the criteria rows "
             "(see dispatch.multi_attribute_summon_cost_is_multiple_rows) plus the count from "
             "0x0225CF28. CONSEQUENCE: reaching 0x0225FA46 with a donor cid + two criteria rows is "
             "the whole of a 'banish 1 LIGHT and 1 DARK from GY' summon condition. NOTE 0x0225CF28 "
             "is itself a per-cid switch (code, not a table); whether it has a usable fall-through "
             "default for an unnamed cid is NOT established — see handss.banish_cost_count_default.",
             "# the cluster's compare base really is Fenrir, and the two leaves are where claimed\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0225E8B0, 'ov3') == 0x1CF8, 'add r0,r7,#3 (Chaos Sorcerer) drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0225E8CE, 'ov3') == 0x1D78, 'add r0,r7,#5 (BLS-Envoy) drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0225E8DA, 'ov3') == 0x371E, 'add r7,#0x1e (CED) drifted'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x0225E8E0, 'ov3') == 0x0225FA46, 'LIGHT+DARK leaf retargeted'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x0225E98E, 'ov3') == 0x0225FA36, 'single-attribute leaf retargeted'\n"
             "# 0x0225FA46 runs pass 0 then pass 1 through the criteria registry, no cid constant\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x0225FA74, 'ov3') == 0x02243FE0, 'pass-0 enumerator retargeted'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x0225FA94, 'ov3') == 0x02243FE0, 'pass-1 enumerator retargeted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0225FA6A, 'ov3') == 0x2100, 'pass index 0 store drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x0225FA8A, 'ov3') == 0x2101, 'pass index 1 store drifted'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x0225FA7C, 'ov3') == 0x0225CF28 and \\\n"
             "       h.bl_target(0x0225FA9C, 'ov3') == 0x0225CF28, 'required-count call retargeted'",
             ["lightpulsar-findings"], addr=0x0225FA46, oracle="ov3")
