             "  (1) ROOT 0x02262962 — selects r5 = HOW MANY CARDS TO SELECT this pass. Family arm "
             "0x02262A5A = `movs r5,#2` (or 1 while [rec+0x28] == 0). Reached by exactly 5 cids, "
             "ALL REAL CARDS: 0x16C9 0x16CB 0x16E4 0x1BC8 0x1BC9. Everything else (6378 cids, incl. "
             "any donor) falls to the default 0x02262AAE, which sets up NO selection.\n"
             "  (2) ROOT 0x02262C24 — THE TWO-PASS DRIVER. Family arm 0x02262C8C does "
             "`[rec+0x28] += 1` and, if the OLD index was 0, `[rec+0x24] = 4` i.e. GO ROUND AGAIN. "
             "THIS IS THE ONLY THING THAT MAKES THE SECOND (DARK) PASS HAPPEN. A donor routed to "
             "the default 0x02262CA4 finishes after one pass.\n"
             "The other two 0x0225CF28 callers need NOTHING — they are cid-generic: 0x0225F678 is a "
             "single-pass count check and 0x02264814 is the 'how many must you banish' prompt, which "
             "merely consumes 0x0225CF28's return. Bounded by scanning ov3 for every literal holding "
             "a family cid and every PC-relative load of one: 28 sites total, only 0x02262974 and "
             "0x02262C26/0x02262C2E in the payment region. ⚠️ HOOK THE ROOTS, NOT THE ARMS: "
             "0x02262C8C's 'both passes done' path branches to 0x02262CA4, so a cid test placed at "
             "0x02262CA4 sends the donor back to 0x02262C8C FOREVER. ⚠️ Only r2 is safe to clobber "
