    S = "leave_field_triggers"
    verified("leave.two_trees_one_function_pick_by_timing", S,
             "*** THE WHOLE PER-CID LEAVE DISPATCH IS ONE FUNCTION WITH TWO cid TREES, AND WHICH "
             "TREE YOU ARM FROM DECIDES WHICH DEPARTURES YOU SEE. Entry 0x021C7FD0 (`push "
             "{r3-r7,lr} ; sub sp,#0x1e8`) has exactly ONE caller in the whole ROM, the guarded "
             "`BL` @0x021CD2AC (guard: `[sp+0x4c]==0 AND ([sp+0x14]!=0 OR r4>0xA)`, "
             "0x021CD28A..0x021CD29A). Inside it are BOTH cid compare trees -- TREE 1 root "
             "0x021C8216 and TREE 2 root 0x021C9F1C -- and the arming gate 0x021CA640, so all "
             "three share ONE stack frame and every descriptor slot is live at any of them. "
             "TREE 1's root is STRAIGHT-LINE FALL-THROUGH from the prologue: every branch in "
             "0x021C7FD0..0x021C8214 lands ON 0x021C8216 (predecessors 0x021C81F6 / 0x021C8206 / "
             "0x021C8210). TREE 2's root has one predecessor, the `beq` @0x021C9F18, plus "
             "fall-through from 0x021C9F1A. *** THE DESCRIPTOR UNPACK (arg 5 at [sp+0x200], "
             "0x021C7FD0..0x021C8054): [sp+0x144] = 1 iff the destination zone field == 0x0E (to "
             "GY); [sp+0x28] = dest == 0x0D; [sp+0x90] = descriptor bit 15 (DESTROYED); [sp+0x44] "
             "= bit 16 (BATTLE); [sp+0x2c] = 1 iff bit 23 is CLEAR; [sp+0x30] = the two side "
             "fields differ. *** THE GATE 0x021CA640 REQUIRES ONLY THREE THINGS to reach its "
             "trigger-build `bl 0x021D2584` @0x021CA686: [sp+0x2c] != 0, r6 == [sp+0x98] "
             "(controller), and [sp+0x144] != 0 (destination is the GY). It does NOT test "
             "DESTROYED or BATTLE -- that arm is the OTHER one at 0x021CA654. So the gate itself "
             "is an ANY-LEAVE-TO-GY gate. *** CONSEQUENCE, AND THE BUG IT EXPLAINS "
             "(card.darksoul_rehome, measured in-game 2026-09-08): the shared T.G. trampoline at "
             "TREE 1 (tg_table._shared_arm_trampoline) adds its OWN `[sp+0x90]` DESTROYED test "
             "before jumping to the gate -- required for T.G. Striker / Warwolf / Rush Rhino and "
             "Quasar, all printed 'destroyed', and its comment records that without it 'Tribute "
             "Summon fodder and Synchro Material also armed the search'. Registering an ANY-LEAVE "
             "card there therefore arms on battle destruction and SILENTLY NOT on Synchro "
             "Material / Tribute. An any-leave card must hook its own trampoline that reaches "
             "0x021CA640 WITHOUT that test; darksoul does it at TREE 2's root 0x021C9F1C "
             "(native `LDR R0,[PC,#0x9C] ; CMP R4,R0`, 4827 4284, literal 0x00001A64 @0x021C9FBC), "
             "which is the position the pre-2026-09-08 Deep Diver build armed from and which the "
             "user confirms worked on Synchro Material. ⚠️ REPLAY ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING at that "
             "site: the replayed `CMP R4,R0` must be the LAST instruction before `BX LR`, because "
             "0x021C9F20 is a `BLE` that consumes those flags. *** IN-GAME CONFIRMED BY USER "
             "2026-09-08: with the arming moved to the tree-2 trampoline the card fires on "
             "Synchro Material AND on battle destruction, with no regression to the four cards "
             "still on the DESTROYED-filtered tree-1 trampoline.",
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x021C9F1C, 4, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('27488442'), \\\n"
             "    'tree 2 root bytes drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u32(0x021C9FBC, 'ov3') == 0x00001A64, 'tree 2 root literal drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021C7FD2, 'ov3') & 0xFF00 == 0xB500, 'leave fn prologue drifted'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021C9F20, 'ov3') & 0xFF00 == 0xDD00, \\\n"
             "    '0x021C9F20 is no longer the BLE that consumes the replayed flags'\n"
             "# the gate's three terms, read as (ldr [sp,#off] ; cmp ; b<cc>) triples\n"
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x021CA640, 4, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('0b980028'), 'gate term 1'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021CA64C, 'ov3') == 0x9851, 'gate term 3 is not ldr r0,[sp,#0x144]'\n"
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x021CA686, 2, 'ov3') != b'\\x00\\x00', 'gate trigger-build call gone'\n",
             ["notes/darksoul-normal-donor-findings.md"],
             addr=0x021C7FD0, oracle="ov3")
