    verified("dispatch.list_a_has_two_inert_members", "effect_dispatch_tables",
             "*** LIST A HAS TWO FREE SLOTS AND LIST B HAS NONE -- which is the difference "
             "between 'a donor can own two criteria rows' and 'it cannot'. Extends "
             "dispatch.two_row_criteria_is_list_b_plus_l2, which documented LIST B as the "
             "two-row list and noted only in passing that two LIST A members have no rows. "
             "LIST A @0x0227134C is 59 sorted u16 (count immediate `MOV R2,#0x3B` @0x02243BF0) "
             "and its rule is `row = (param != 0) ? 1 : 0` (CMP R4,#0 @0x02243BFA) -- simpler "
             "than LIST B's `param & 0x10000000`, and satisfied by ANY nonzero param, so a card "
             "using LIST A does NOT need L2 membership. Exactly two of its members own ZERO "
             "criteria rows: Speed Spell - Preparation of Rites 0x0D7A and Speed Spell - "
             "Stardust Shimmer 0x0D81. A cid with no rows never reaches the row-offset "
             "computation at all, so their membership is vestigial and either may be dropped "
             "count-neutrally to admit a new two-row cid. "
             "⚠️ AVAILABILITY, AS OF 2026-08-30: ONLY 0x0D81 IS STILL FREE. 0x0D7A HAS BEEN SPENT "
             "by card.snoww_clause2 (ledger: {pool: membership_list_a, cid: 0x0D7A, owner: "
             "snoww}). So LIST A now has exactly ONE slot left, and it is the last one -- the "
             "next two-row card after that must either displace a real member or find another "
             "route to row 1. This availability half is a LEDGER question, NOT a ROM question: "
             "the proof below runs against the COMMITTED ov3 oracle, which is the STOCK image "
             "where both cids are still row-less, so it can NEVER catch a slot being spent. "
             "ALWAYS re-read docs/engine/allocations.yaml before claiming one. "
             "By contrast EVERY LIST B member owns "
             "exactly 2 rows, and its only phantom 0x234F is already spent by "
             "card.gates_of_dark_world. *** WHY THIS MATTERS FOR COMPOSITION: reaching row 1 via "
             "LIST A + a cid-scoped trampoline on a step's own param provider avoids L2 "
             "entirely, and L2's lookup `bl 0x02022E14` @0x02234E96 is ALREADY hijacked by "
             "Gates of Dark World's CAVE_GDW_L2 stub.",
             """
             from collections import Counter
             B, CNT = 0x022713C4, 0x56C
             cnt = Counter(h.u16(B + i * 12, 'ov3') for i in range(CNT))
             la = h.u16_table(0x0227134C, 59, 'ov3')
             lb = h.u16_table(0x02271314, 27, 'ov3')
             assert h.u16(0x02243BF0, 'ov3') == 0x223B, 'the LIST A count immediate is not MOV R2,#0x3B'
             assert h.u16(0x02243C06, 'ov3') == 0x221B, 'the LIST B count immediate is not MOV R2,#0x1B'
             assert h.u16(0x02243BFA, 'ov3') == 0x2C00, "LIST A's rule is no longer CMP R4,#0"
             assert h.is_sorted_unique(la) and h.is_sorted_unique(lb), 'a membership list lost its order'
             inert = [c for c in la if cnt[c] == 0]
             assert inert == [0x0D7A, 0x0D81], \\
                 f'LIST A inert members are {[hex(c) for c in inert]}, expected 0x0D7A/0x0D81'
             assert all(cnt[c] == 2 for c in lb), \\
                 f'a LIST B member no longer owns exactly 2 rows: '\\
                 f'{[(hex(c), cnt[c]) for c in lb if cnt[c] != 2]}'
             assert 0x234F in lb or 0x1C8B in lb, 'LIST B lost both its phantom and the Gates donor'
             """,
             ["notes/snoww-findings.md", "notes/gates-of-dark-world-findings.md"],
             addr=0x0227134C, oracle="ov3")
