    verified("event.animation_command_dispatcher", S,
             "The animation/relocation command queue (event.animation_command_queue) is DRAINED "
             "by a jump-table dispatcher at 0x021C3C3C: `op = [0x02299B60] & 0xFFF`, bounded "
             "`cmp op,#0x68`, halfword offset table at 0x021C3C5E based at 0x021C3C60, and each "
             "arm is a 6-byte `bl <handler> ; pop {r3,pc}` stub. THIS is where a queued command "
             "becomes a state change, which is why neither 0x021C6B00 nor 0x021C7118 nor "
             "0x021D1300 contains any array write. Decoded opcodes: 0x1E->0x021BC254, "
             "0x1F->0x021BC274, 0x20->0x021BC3EC, 0x26->0x021C3B70, 0x32->0x021BF884 (banish), "
             "0x3E->0x021BC4B8 (zone-to-zone relocate), 0x40->0x021BCCDC, 0x45->0x021BF5E4, "
             "0x52->0x021C1BB0, **0x55->0x021C0BB4 = THE DECK SHUFFLE** (which calls the "
             "Fisher-Yates permutation 0x021A7B7C(side) over player+0x304, count player+0x10, "
             "swapping through 0x021A1F9C, then raises UI code 0x15).\n"
             "*** ⚠️⚠️ CONSEQUENCE — 0x021D269C IS 'SHUFFLE THE DECK', NOT 'COMPLETION'. It "
             "builds `r0 = 0x55 | (side ? 0x8000 : 0)`, passes the RNG state from "
             "[0x0229DD14+0x28] as the arguments (so a replay reproduces the permutation), and "
             "enqueues it. It sits at the end of the native add-to-hand resolver 0x02207EF5 and "
             "of Gold Sarcophagus 0x0221CD29 because BOTH SEARCH THE DECK, where shuffling is "
             "correct — that is how it got mislabelled as a phase-0x64 'completion' primitive "
             "(from the 3DS mapping 0x388E3C -> 0x021D269C) and copied into four patch modules "
             "as COMPLETE / EFFECT_DONE. MEASURED: Eclipse Wyvern's clause 2 moves a card from "
             "the banished zone to the hand and touched no Deck, yet the deck came out as the "
             "same multiset in a different order on our side only, across three builds — it "
             "survived removing the prompt, which is what isolated this call. A resolver phase "
             "does NOT need it; dropping it ends the phase cleanly.",
             "# the dispatcher's bound and jump-table geometry\n"
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x021C3C4C, 4, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('6828 00d9'.replace(' ', '')), \\\n"
             "    'the command dispatcher bound (op <= 0x68) drifted'\n"
             "def _arm(op):\n"
             "    e = h.u16(0x021C3C5E + op * 2, 'ov3')\n"
             "    return 0x021C3C60 + (e if e < 0x8000 else e - 0x10000)\n"
             "assert _arm(0x55) == 0x021C3F28, f'opcode 0x55 arm moved to {_arm(0x55):#010x}'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021C3F28) == 0x021C0BB4, 'the 0x55 handler is no longer 0x021C0BB4'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021C0C20) == 0x021A7B7C, 'the 0x55 handler no longer shuffles'\n"
             "assert _arm(0x3E) == 0x021C3E9E and h.bl_target(0x021C3E9E) == 0x021BC4B8, \\\n"
             "    'the relocate (0x3E) arm drifted'\n"
             "assert _arm(0x32) == 0x021C3E56, 'the banish (0x32) arm drifted'\n"
             "# 0x021D269C builds opcode 0x55 and enqueues it -- it is a shuffle, not a completion\n"
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x021D26AE, 4, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('55200843'), \\\n"
             "    '0x021D269C no longer builds command 0x55'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021D26C2) == 0x021C3BC8, '0x021D269C no longer enqueues'\n"
             "# and the shuffle itself is Fisher-Yates over the deck container\n"
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x021A7B92, 4, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('c1208000'), \\\n"
             "    'the shuffle no longer indexes player+0x304'\n",
             ["eclipse-wyvern-findings"], addr=0x021C3C3C, oracle="ov3")
