             "on 0x021AFCBC(desc, side, zone) != 0, computes r1 = (side == desc[+2]) ? 0 : 1 (mine vs "
             "the opponent's), and tail-calls 0x021C5358(side, zone, r3, [sp+0x20], [sp] = cid, "
             "[sp+4] = r1). No position is ever passed, so what it does is flip. CONSEQUENCE: the 16 "
             "native cards on resolver 0x0220C6B1 can only ever do Attack -> Defense, because they "
             "hardcode r4 = 1 (except Reptilianne Naga 0x21B4, r4 = 0) and pair it with the "
             "Attack-Position-only condition 0x021F4D4D. A card whose text is the unqualified 'change "
             "the battle position of this card' (Maiden with Eyes of Blue) must therefore NOT clone "
             "0x0220C6B0 -- it should call 0x021C5324 outright after 0x021D2C1C (still on the field) "
             "and 0x021D2D18 (re-sync desc[+2]/desc[+3] from the locator desc[+0xC]), which is both "
             "simpler and more faithful than the native shape. *** STACK ABI TRAP: the 5th argument "
             "is passed in the caller's [sp], so the caller's prologue must PUSH A SCRATCH LOW "
             "REGISTER FIRST to reserve that word -- 0x0220C6B0's `push {r3,r4,r5,r6,r7,lr}` is "
             "reserving, not saving (Thumb PUSH stores the lowest-numbered register at the lowest "
             "address).",
