    savestate("ram.graveyard_and_banished_arrays", S,
              "Graveyard = player+0x55C, count = player+0x14. Banished ('removed from play') = "
              "player+0x7B4, count = player+0x1C. Both are PACKED u32 card-word arrays with the "
              "same shape as the Extra Deck (+0x4E4 / count +0x18): the first `count` words are "
              "the live entries. ⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-08-13: the original wording added 'then zeros', "
              "and that is FALSE — a REMOVAL shifts the survivors down but leaves the old tail "
              "word in place, so there can be stale nonzero words past `count`. Counter-example "
              "in rom_all_patches.ml2: side-0 GY has count 2 but words [0x14002387, 0x08001859, "
              "0x08001859] — the third is a duplicate ghost of the second. ALWAYS trust the count, "
              "never the nonzero span (this is exactly how a banished-zone reader would silently "
              "pick up a card that is no longer there). Found by diffing sealancer_recon.ml6 (Mermaid Archer "
              "0x1FFC on the field, equipped with Deep Sea Diva 0x1FFB) against .ml7 (Mermaid "
              "Archer banished): 0x1FFC appeared at player+0x7B4 with +0x1C going 0->1, while the "
              "equipped Diva was appended to the GY at player+0x578 with +0x14 going 7->8. The "
              "invariant was then checked over 5 savestates x 2 players = 20 cases, all clean. "
              "This is what a 'target your banished monsters' effect (Sea Lancer E1) must "
              "enumerate — the equip-target selector 0x0224FA4C/0x0225028E only sweeps monster "
              "zones 5..9, so E1 is NOT reachable by swapping that leaf's predicate.",
              "base, stride = 0x0229AC94, 0xB3C\n"
              "for side in (0, 1):\n"
              "    pb = base + side * stride\n"
              "    for name, arr, cnt, cap in (('GY', 0x55C, 0x14, 60), ('banished', 0x7B4, 0x1C, 60)):\n"
              "        n = h.ram_u32(pb + cnt)\n"
              "        assert 0 <= n <= cap, f'{name} count {n} out of range for side {side}'\n"
              "        words = [h.ram_u32(pb + arr + i * 4) for i in range(cap)]\n"
              "        lead = [w for w in words[:n] if w == 0]\n"
              "        assert not lead, f'{name} side {side}: hole inside the first {n} entries'\n"
              "        # every LIVE entry must decode to a plausible cid on the owning side\n"
              "        for i, w in enumerate(words[:n]):\n"
              "            assert 0x0B00 < (w & 0x3FFF) < 0x2600, \\\n"
              "                f'{name} side {side}[{i}] = {w:#010x} is not a card word'\n"
              "        # NOT asserted: zeros past the count. Removals leave stale ghost words\n"
              "        # (see the correction in the claim) — the count is the only truth.\n",
              ["sea-lancer-findings"], addr=0x0229AC94, conf="VERIFIED")
