             "(the `cmp rX,#1` / `cmp rX,#-1` then `muls` idiom at 0x021B60E8 and 0x021B611E); a "
             "literal delta is applied as-is. 45 of table 2's rows carry the sentinel and are "
             "exactly the 'gains N ATK for each X' cards (Chaosrider Gustaph, Card Trooper, "
             "Necroface, ...), while fixed-delta rows match their printed text (Zombyra -200, "
             "Exarion Universe -400, Legendary Fiend +700, Insect Princess +500). "
             "⚠ CORRECTED 2026-08-03: table 2 was recorded as 0x0226E4BC/103 rows, which is TEN "
             "ROWS TOO HIGH -- it came from a manual walk that started mid-array. The consumer's own "
             "immediates are `movs r2,#0x71` @0x021B60BA and `movs r3,#6` @0x021B60BC with the base "
             "literal at 0x021B6184, and 0x0226E480 + 113*6 = 0x0226E726 while table 1 ends exactly "
             "at 0x0226E47E. The old fact still PASSed because a subrange of a sorted array is still "
             "sorted and all three spot-checked rows lay inside it -- the proof below now pins both "
             "bases to the consumer's literals so the same mistake cannot pass again. "
             "⚠ These tables are NOT where a continuous 'gains N ATK for each X' effect lives: "
             "every one of table 2's 51 sentinel rows is an activated or event-driven gain, and the "
             "amount is frozen at attach time. See stat.recompute for the continuous engine.",
             "assert h.u32(0x021B6188, 'ov3') == 0x0226E1E4, 'delta table 1 base literal moved'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021B610C, 'ov3') == 0x226F, 'table 1 count is not movs r2,#0x6f'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021B610E, 'ov3') == 0x2306, 'table 1 stride is not movs r3,#6'\n"
             "assert h.u32(0x021B6184, 'ov3') == 0x0226E480, 'delta table 2 base literal moved'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021B60BA, 'ov3') == 0x2271, 'table 2 count is not movs r2,#0x71'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021B60BC, 'ov3') == 0x2306, 'table 2 stride is not movs r3,#6'\n"
