    verified("counter.capacity_gate", S,
             "⚠️ THE GATE THAT ACTUALLY DECIDES WHETHER A COUNTER IS PLACED. "
             "0x021C7D80 does NOT place blindly: at 0x021C7D8C it reads the current count via "
             "0x021A3054(side, zone, type) and at 0x021C7DD0 it reads the CAPACITY via "
             "0x021A2F10(side, zone, type), returning 0 (placing nothing) when the capacity is 0 "
             "or already reached. 0x021A2F10 switches on the counter TYPE; each arm is a "
             "hard-coded per-cid chain over the cid of the card in that zone (from 0x021A36F8). "
             "The TYPE 6 (Bushido) arm starts at 0x021A2F9E: 0x1D22 Six Samurai United -> 2 "
             "(this, NOT a separate clause, is that card's printed '(max. 2)'), 0x219A Gateway "
             "of the Six -> 0xFF, 0x247E Temple of the Six -> 0xFF, anything else -> 0. "
             "CONSEQUENCE FOR PATCHING: a donor given a registry row AND an arm call still "
             "accrues NOTHING until it also has a capacity entry. Measured in-game both ways: "
             "Shien's Dojo accumulated no counters with the row+arm correct, and accumulated "
             "correctly once a capacity entry was added (shiens_dojo PART E). So the "
             "COMPLETE recipe for 'card X accrues counters of type T' is THREE things: a "
             "registry row @0x02275510 pointing at a type-T thunk, an arm call in the "
             "event-gated branch, and a capacity entry in 0x021A2F10's type-T arm. "
             "Other type arms "
             "grant capacity by archetype predicate instead of a cid literal (type 1 calls the "
             "ARM9 thunk 0x0202352C).",
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021C7D8C, 'ov3') == 0x021A3054, 'current-count call moved'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021C7DD0, 'ov3') == 0x021A2F10, 'capacity call moved'\n"
             "# the type-6 chain: {cid literal, capacity immediate} x 3\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021A2F9E, 'ov3') == 0x4926, 'type-6 chain head is not the LDR'\n"
             "for pool, cid, imm_at, cap in ((0x021A3038, 0x1D22, 0x021A2FA4, 0x02),\n"
             "                               (0x021A303C, 0x219A, 0x021A2FAE, 0xFF),\n"
             "                               (0x021A3040, 0x247E, 0x021A2FB8, 0xFF)):\n"
             "    assert h.u32(pool, 'ov3') == cid, f'capacity chain literal {pool:#x} drifted'\n"
             "    hw = h.u16(imm_at, 'ov3')\n"
             "    assert (hw >> 11) == 0b00100 and ((hw >> 8) & 7) == 0 and (hw & 0xFF) == cap, \\\n"
             "        f'capacity immediate at {imm_at:#x} is not MOV R0,#{cap:#x}'\n",
             ["notes/shiens-dojo-findings.md"], addr=0x021A2F10, oracle="ov3")
