             "`ldr r2,=0x0FB6`, `movs r3,#2`, `bl 0x021C479C` -- the attached-node writer. Because "
             "the key is side + SLOT it is scoped to ONE monster in ONE zone. *** IT PAIRS WITH A "
             "QUERY ALREADY PRESENT IN THE NATIVE IGNITION CONDITION: the ignition-condition "
             "registry row\'s f1 for Beast Striker 0x20B8 is 0x021F024D, whose first act is "
             "`ldrb r0,[r5,#2] ; ldrb r1,[r5,#3] ; ldr r2,=0x0FB6 ; bl 0x021A1430` -- the same "
             "side + slot + key. So a donor that takes Beast Striker\'s registry row and posts "
             "this tag from its cost gets \'once per turn, per copy\' with NO condition stub of its "
             "own: the stock 0x021F0BDD does the whole check. *** MEASURED THE HARD WAY: with the "
             "cid-keyed turn log instead, in-game test 2 on card.upstart_golden_ninja showed a "
             "second copy Special Summoned by the first having NO effect entry in its menu "
             "(rom_upstart.ml4 has both donors on the field). ⚠️ NOT VERIFIABLE IN THE SAVESTATE "
             "EMULATOR: the attach 0x021C479C is reached (traced) and 0x021E5060 returns 1, but "
             "the following 0x021A1430 query still reads 0, because the post is an event-queue "
             "operation a static run does not settle -- the identical limitation was confirmed "
             "with Pot of Duality 0x2321 as a native control for the turn-log pair.",
             "# the tag keys on side + SLOT, which is what makes it per copy\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021E5070, 'ov3') == 0x78A0, '0x021E5070 is no longer ldrb r0,[r4,#2]'\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021E5072, 'ov3') == 0x78E1, '0x021E5072 is no longer ldrb r1,[r4,#3]'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021E5078, 'ov3') == 0x021C479C, 'the node attach moved'\n"
             "# ... and the native ignition condition f1 queries exactly that key\n"
             "assert h.u16(0x021F0252, 'ov3') == 0x78A8, '0x021F0252 is no longer ldrb r0,[r5,#2]'\n"
