             "exceptions. Row layout: {+0x00 u16 cid, +0x02 u16 filter value (a SET CODE "
             "normally, a CID when flags has 0x0800 'by name', 0xFFFF = no archetype filter), "
             "+0x04 u32 Thumb handler, +0x08 u16 flags, +0x0A u16 extra}. The +0x0A LOW BYTE is "
             "the LEVEL BOUND, encoded 0x80 | (L << 2): 0x88=Lv<=2, 0x8C=Lv<=3, 0x90=Lv<=4, "
             "0x94=5, 0x98=6, 0x9C=7, 0xA0=8, 0x00 = no bound; the high byte is a Type/race "
             "filter. **CONFIRMED IN-GAME**: with a donor row carrying 0x0090 the card summons "
             "Level<=4 monsters and REFUSES Level 5+ (shiens_dojo clause 2). ⚠️ Note for "
             "anyone auditing this: NONE of the three thin criteria handlers (0x0223CAB4, "
             "0x0223CAF4, 0x0223E31C) reads +0x0A — each touches only +0x00/+0x02/+0x08 — so a "
             "static read of the handlers looks like the field is unused. It is consumed "
             "DOWNSTREAM, by the worker 0x0223BC3C / its callback, which is what actually walks "
             "the Deck. 'The immediate caller does not read it' is NOT evidence a field is dead. "
             "Worked examples (byte facts, independently cross-validated against the 3DS build): "
             "Shien's Footsoldier 0x1B3A = "
             "{001E, 0x0223CAB5, 0002, 008C} = 'set code 0x1E (Six Samurai), Level <= 3'; "
             "Six Scrolls 0x1F76 = {1B39, 0x0223D075, 0802, 0000} = 'the card NAMED Great Shogun "
             "Shien'. To give a donor a filtered Deck search, insert a row here (count-neutral: "
             "the array is sorted with a hard count).",
             "base, cnt = 0x022713C4, 1388\n"
             "cids = [h.u16(base + i * 12, 'ov3') for i in range(cnt)]\n"
             "assert all(cids[i] <= cids[i+1] for i in range(cnt-1)), 'criteria registry not sorted'\n"
             "rows = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(cids)}\n"
             "for cid, filt, hand, flags, extra in (\n"
             "        (0x1B3A, 0x001E, 0x0223CAB5, 0x0002, 0x008C),\n"
             "        (0x247B, 0x001E, 0x0223CAF5, 0x0002, 0x008C),\n"
             "        (0x1F76, 0x1B39, 0x0223D075, 0x0802, 0x0000)):\n"
             "    i = rows[cid]\n"
             "    assert h.u16(base + i * 12 + 2, 'ov3') == filt\n"
             "    assert h.u32(base + i * 12 + 4, 'ov3') == hand\n"
             "    assert h.u16(base + i * 12 + 8, 'ov3') == flags\n"
             "    assert h.u16(base + i * 12 + 10, 'ov3') == extra\n"
             "seen = set()\n"
             "for i in range(cnt):\n"
             "    lo = h.u16(base + i * 12 + 10, 'ov3') & 0xFF\n"
             "    if lo & 0x80:\n"
             "        lvl = (lo & 0x7F) >> 2\n"
             "        assert 1 <= lvl <= 12, f'row {i} low byte {lo:#04x} is not a level'\n"
             "        seen.add(lvl)\n"
             "assert {2, 3, 4} <= seen, f'expected Lv<=2/3/4 bounds, got {sorted(seen)}'\n",
