             "0x02235632's `CMP R0,#0 ; BNE` took the `movs r0,#1 ; pop` = SKIP exit. Native "
             "Goldd offering in the same duel was the tell: its targets are on the FIELD, not in "
             "a Graveyard. Rebuilding the harness at 8 copies fixed it. ROUND 2 'target selected "
             "but nothing summoned' WAS a patch bug, and the fix is the reusable lesson: see "
             "dispatch.pick_record_and_resolver_readback -- the declared-pick count for the "
             "SHARED off-field picker is the byte desc[+0x10], NOT [0x0229AAFC+0x74]. The latter "
             "is private to Goldd's own bespoke slot5 step machine and is written NOWHERE on the "
             "shared-picker path (scanned every `STR Rn,[Rm,#0x74]` in ov3: none inside "
             "0x0223847C..0x02238560 nor 0x02235604..0x02235800). CLONING A NATIVE CARD IS ONLY "
             "SAFE FIELD BY FIELD: the skeleton was right, but one of its reads belonged to a "
             "component that had been swapped out, and the replacement keeps its state elsewhere. "
             "Re-derive every value the surrounding code reads; never inherit them.\n"
             "*** CLAUSE 2 IS A STRUCTURAL CLONE OF GOLDD, WU-LORD OF DARK WORLD 0x1969, whose "
             "PRINTED TEXT is identical in shape ('...you can target up to 2 cards your opponent "
             "controls; Special Summon this card from the Graveyard, then destroy those targets "
             "(if any)'). Goldd cls2[192] = {+04 0x0221FB51, +08 0x021DE7C9, +0C 0x0224A115, "
             "+10 0, +14 0x0223847D}, and TWO of its pieces are the whole design: (i) its "
             "RESOLVER 0x0221FB50 is a two-phase machine -- phase 0x80 runs the base action then "
             "returns 0x7F iff [0x0229AAFC+0x74] (THE DECLARED-TARGET COUNTER = the printed 'if "
             "any') is nonzero, phase 0x7F runs the targeted action and returns 0; (ii) its SLOT5 "
             "0x0223847C STEP 0 is the opponent gate AND the 'you can' prompt, returning 1 to "
             "SKIP. *** THAT CORRECTS event.optional_trigger_is_record_shape's warning as I first "
             "read it: a HALF-optional card does NOT need branching slot3/slot4 stubs. Goldd's "
             "slot3 is the generic 0x0224A115 and its slot4 is 0; the optionality lives in slot5, "
             "which is skipped wholesale when the gate fails.\n"
             "*** SNOWW'S CLAUSE 2 = 3 ov5 stubs + 3 data edits. cls2 becomes {+04 CAVE_SNOWW_RES, "
             "+08 0, +0C 0x0224A115, +10 0, +14 CAVE_SNOWW_SLOT5}. CAVE_SNOWW_RES is Goldd's "
             "skeleton with clause 1 grafted in: phase 0x7F -> 0x02204730(desc, 1, 1) = Special "
             "Summon the recorded pick in FACE-UP DEFENSE (r2 is the position, saved to [sp+8]; "
             "the r5 inside 0x02204730 is an unrelated local), otherwise delegate to 0x02207EF4 "
             "and, when it returns 0 with a target declared, return 0x7F. THE GRAFT IS PROVABLY "
             "SAFE: phase 0x7F is UNUSED by 0x02207EF5 (its jump table reads from 0x02207FEE but "
             "branches from 0x02207FF0 -- a two-byte difference that points every arm one "
             "halfword early if you get it wrong -- and entry 7 lands on a bare `movs r0,#0 ; "
             "pop`), and 0x02207EF4 never reads or writes [0x0229AAFC+0x74] anywhere in its "
             "extent. CAVE_SNOWW_SLOT5 is Goldd's step-0 gate then a TAIL-CALL to the native "
             "off-field picker 0x02235604, stateless so it consumes no step of [0x0229AB7C]. "
             "CAVE_SNOWW_ROW cid-scopes slot5's own `bl 0x02234E78` @0x02235610 to return 1 for "
             "the donor, so LIST A's `row = (param != 0)` gives slot5 ROW 1 while the add-to-hand "
             "resolver's separate provider call @0x02208028 still returns 0 = ROW 0. THE EMPTY-GY "
             "GUARD IS STRUCTURAL, not synthesised: 0x02235632 `CMP R0,#0 ; BNE` sends a "
             "zero-candidate enumeration to `movs r0,#1 ; pop` = skip.\n"
             "*** DATA: criteria ROW 1 {0x1C18, 0xFFFF, 0x0223E1D1, 0x00010002} inserted ADJACENT "
             "to and AFTER row 0 (count-neutral over phantom 0x14EF), and LIST A membership "
             "count-neutral over the inert 0x0D7A -- NOT LIST B, which is full and whose phantom "
             "and L2 lookup both belong to gates_of_dark_world.\n"
             "*** ⚠️ ONE GAP FOUND IN-GAME, AND IT IS NOT THIS CARD'S: 'The Gates of Dark World' "
             "itself CANNOT BE FETCHED by the search, because the Gates donor Colosseum 0x1C8B "
