    verified("dispatch.ov3_switch_stubs_must_register", S,
             "*** EVERY PATCH THAT PLANTS AN ov3 STUB ON THE 0x021D1392 PER-CID CHAIN MUST "
             "DECLARE IT VIA snoww.register_switch_stub AT IMPORT TIME, OR IT SILENTLY "
             "BREAKS THE COMBINED BUILD. *** snoww's _assert_switch_unchanged walks all "
             "0x2700 cids and compares each one's leaf against the committed ov3 oracle. Its "
             "tracer _switch_leaf stops at any BL it does not recognise as a REGISTERED stub, so "
             "every cid that merely PASSES THROUGH some other patch's stub reads as 'changed "
             "leaf' and the build aborts. *** MEASURED 2026-08-28, on the first full "
             "apply_all_patches run since card.snoww_unlight_of_dark_world shipped: the chain died "
             "at step 30 (Snoww) with `AssertionError: R cid 0x17C6 changed leaf: 0x021D19C0 -> "
             "0x021B5920`. 0x021B5920 is card.eclipse_wyvern's GATE_STUB, planted at step 25, five "
             "steps earlier -- Eclipse predates the register_switch_stub mechanism and never "
             "called it, so the breakage had been latent in the chain the whole time and was NOT "
             "caused by the card being shipped that day (card.grapha_clause3, step 31, had not yet "
             "run). ⚠️ THE LESSON IS ABOUT DETECTION, NOT ABOUT EITHER CARD: a composition guard "
             "that only runs in the FULL chain is not exercised by any single-card _build_*.py, so "
             "it can stay red for as long as nobody ships. Run apply_all_patches when you add a "
             "patch that touches SHARED ov3 code, not only when you ship. *** THE FIX is one "
             "import-time line and EMITS NO BYTES -- it only populates the tracer's tables: "
             "`_snoww.register_switch_stub(GATE_STUB, GATE_STUB_LEN, {DONOR_CID: <terminus>})`. "
             "⚠️ THE TERMINUS IS NOT ALWAYS THE ARM: _switch_leaf follows a DIRECT BL (what "
             "grapha's stub uses, so its donor registers as the real arm 0x021D185C) but "
             "COULD NOT originally resolve a PC-relative literal through a register, so "
             "Eclipse's `LDR R0,[PC,#4] ; BX R0` tail terminated the walk at the BX itself and its "
             "donor had to be registered as GATE_STUB + 14 -- an address INSIDE its own stub, "
             "which made the guard check 'the walk stopped where we expected' rather than 'the "
             "donor reaches the right arm'. *** FIXED PROPERLY 2026-08-28: _switch_leaf now "
             "follows an indirect tail, but ONLY when the BX is inside a REGISTERED stub, where "
             "the register value provably came from a literal load out of the same overlay image "
             "rather than from unmodelled code -- so the tracer's conservatism everywhere else is "
             "untouched and no other patch's reported leaf can move. Eclipse's donor now traces "
             "through GATE_ACCEPT to 0x021D19BE `STR R0,[SP,#0x14]`, the ACCEPT path's flag store, "
             "which is a MEANINGFUL terminus: reject cids stop two bytes later at SWITCH_END "
             "0x021D19C0 `MOVS R0,#0`, so the guard now genuinely distinguishes accept from "
             "reject. ⚠️ _switch_leaf is ANALYSIS ONLY and never writes ROM bytes -- the combined "
             "ROM's sha256 was 4c5cf154... before and after this change. *** ⚠️ THE SAME "
             "REGISTRATION-IS-AN-IMPORT-SIDE-EFFECT PROPERTY BIT A SECOND TIME, IN THE VERIFY "
             "SWEEP: _verify_all_patches.py imported each module lazily inside its verify loop, so "
             "whether a stub was registered depended on SHIPPED's ORDERING. snoww sits "
             "before grapha in that list, so Snoww verified while Grapha's stub was still "
             "unregistered and reported a phantom whole-table regression against a ROM that was "
             "correct -- the same walk PASSES the moment both modules are imported. The sweep now "
             "imports EVERY module first and verifies afterwards. GENERAL RULE: when a module "
             "publishes shared state as an import side effect, any harness that loads modules "
             "one-at-a-time will see a partially-populated world, and the symptom is a failure in "
             "some OTHER module that looks like a real regression.",
             """
             from otn_enhanced.cards import eclipse_wyvern as E
             from otn_enhanced.cards import grapha as G
             from otn_enhanced.cards import snoww as S
             # both ov3-stub patches declare themselves to the tracer
             regs = dict(S.EXTRA_SWITCH_STUBS)
             assert regs.get(E.GATE_STUB) == E.GATE_STUB_LEN, \
                 'Eclipse Wyvern no longer registers its switch stub'
             assert regs.get(G.ARM_STUB) == G.ARM_STUB_LEN, \
                 'Grapha no longer registers its switch stub'
             # and their donor termini are the two DIFFERENT shapes described above
             assert S.EXTRA_SWITCH_DONORS[G.DONOR_CID] == G.DW_ARM, \
                 'the direct-BL donor no longer registers as the real arm'
             assert S.EXTRA_SWITCH_DONORS[E.DONOR_CID] == E.GATE_ACCEPT_LEAF, \
                 'the indirect-BX donor terminus moved'
             # the tracer follows the indirect tail through to the ACCEPT flag store,
             # which must stay DISTINCT from the reject leaf two bytes later
             assert E.GATE_ACCEPT_LEAF == S.SWITCH_END - 2, \
                 'the accept terminus is no longer adjacent to the reject leaf'
             # the indirect tail really is LDR R0,[PC,#4] ; BX R0 into GATE_ACCEPT | 1
             import struct
             blob = E._gate_stub(E.GATE_STUB)
             assert struct.unpack_from('<H', blob, 12)[0] == 0x4801, 'the ldr r0,[pc,#4] moved'
             assert struct.unpack_from('<H', blob, 14)[0] == 0x4700, 'the bx r0 moved'
             assert struct.unpack_from('<I', blob, 20)[0] == (E.GATE_ACCEPT | 1), \
                 'the indirect literal is no longer GATE_ACCEPT | 1'
             """,
             ["notes/grapha-findings.md"],
             addr=0x021B5920, oracle="ov3")

