    verified('card.jet_synchron_clause2', 'cards',
             '*** JET SYNCHRON CLAUSES 2 AND 3 ARE IN-GAME CONFIRMED BY THE USER 2026-09-03, on the first test of the full card, against rom_jet_synchron.nds sha256 4871e198ca522130e0abcb166649a6e67d906331795dc1f2226b623d4a93439a. Asked specifically whether they had seen the three items that could each have failed independently, they answered \'yes to all\': (a) CLAUSE 1 STILL SEARCHES after the timing-class hook -- no \'missed the timing\'; (b) CLAUSE 3 locks BOTH clauses to one use per turn while DECLINING a prompt burns nothing; (c) the copy summoned by clause 2 is BANISHED, not sent to the GY, when it leaves the field. Then: \'Ship it!\' -- wired into apply_all_patches the same day. *** CLAUSE 2 = \'If this card is in your GY: You can send 1 card from your hand to the GY; Special Summon this card, but banish it when it leaves the field.\' CLAUSE 3 = \'You can only use 1 "Jet Synchron" effect per turn, and only once that turn.\' Donor Changer Synchron 0x224C, on the SAME cls2 record 555 as card.jet_synchron_clause1. *** ARCHITECTURE A -- ONE SHARED cls2 RECORD, THREE SLOTS BECOME ov5 DISPATCHERS (+04 resolver, +0C condition, +10 activation procedure; +08 and +14 stay 0, because both clauses want the engine\'s own null-slot behaviour). This is lightpulsar\'s structure with the roles swapped. *** THE DISCRIMINATOR IS LIGHTPULSAR\'S CONSTANT VERBATIM -- `desc[+3] == 0x0E && desc[+4] > 6` selects clause 1 -- and the 2026-09-02 handoff was WRONG to call it \'actively unsafe\'. Its worry was that the event-code array 0x0229ABB4 is never cleared, so a stale Special-Summon code 0x09 sitting at index 0 during a GY ignition would satisfy `> 6` and misroute clause 2 into clause 1\'s arm. IT CANNOT: dispatch.gy_action_offer_caps_the_event_code proves the off-field offer gate REFUSES any GY-action descriptor above 6, so with a stale code the effect is simply not offered. The other direction is closed by the producers -- a class-2 descriptor with zone 0x0E reaching this record comes only from the leave / relocation path, which posts 0x17 / 0x1D / 0x1E. *** THE PARTS: (E) the three slot dispatchers; (F) a SECOND criteria row {0x224C, aux 0xFFFF, 0x0223CB19 select-from-HAND, flags 0x000E} -- Plaguespreader Zombie\'s own row 766 with the cid changed, i.e. \'any 1 card in your hand\', which is the printed cost -- inserted IMMEDIATELY AFTER clause 1\'s Deck row, count-neutral over phantom 0x0E4A, with the ORDER ASSERTED because rel 0 must stay the Deck row (dispatch.offer_check_probes_rel0_only); (G) the GY-action registry\'s LAST free phantom row, 48 / 0x0E64, which is what makes the effect offerable from the GY at all; (H) an arm on the SHARED criteria_row_hook keyed on the cost machine\'s own state word [0x0229AAFC+0x7C] -- rel 1 while the cost runs, rel 0 otherwise: the card.upstart_golden_ninja pattern, but with NO probe flag, because this card\'s condition reads the hand COUNT at player+0x0C directly instead of probing a criteria row; (T) an arm on the NEW SHARED timing_class_hook; (P) five ov5 stubs; (R) the rider hook. *** WHY THE TIMING HOOK IS MANDATORY, AND WHY IT HAD TO BECOME SHARED: +0x10 is ALSO the timing-class literal, read RAW by the classifier 0x0224AF7C, and clause 2 must put a real cost function there -- so without an arm clause 1 lands in NO timing class and its trigger evaporates silently. maiden_eyes_of_blue gets away with the same query/stamp split and no hook only because its record is cls3 and 0x0224AF7C returns 0 at once for classes 0 and 3; ours is cls2. The site 0x0224AF96 is a SINGLE 4-byte BL that lightpulsar already owned, so PART T was lifted into timing_class_hook.py with a cid register -- the criteria_row_hook precedent exactly -- and the lift was proven behaviour-preserving BY EXECUTION rather than by argument (scratch/timing_hook_equiv.py runs 30 600 inputs through both emitted stubs and finds ZERO differences on cid 0x0FB1). The row hook\'s new arm got the same treatment (scratch/rowhook_equiv.py: 20 160 inputs, zero differences on 0x0FB1 / 0x1646 / 0x1464). *** THE COST is a re-implementation of Plaguespreader Zombie\'s 0x021E9038 (dispatch.hand_cost_machine_0x021E9038) with ONE semantic change -- the mover 0x021C6988 (hand -> DECK) becomes 0x021C6DB4 (hand -> GY, kind 1 = COST) -- and with the per-cid switch collapsed to PLAGUESPREADER\'s constants rather than the default arm\'s, so the phase-2 0x021D26CC broadcast is skipped exactly as it is for the exemplar. The Graverobber 0x1379 sub-clause is reproduced verbatim (grep-the-template-cards-text-too). ⚠️ THE PACKED CARD REFERENCE IS COMPUTED BEFORE THE MOVER RUNS -- after it the card has left the hand array and the picked index no longer identifies it. The native does the same, and an earlier draft of the stub had the two the other way round until the mandatory disassemble-the-built-stub review caught it. *** CLAUSE 3 IS ONE cid-KEYED TURN-LOG STAMP locking both clauses: the QUERY lives in +0C and the STAMP in +10 (dispatch.once_per_turn_must_stamp_at_activation -- a stamp written in the resolver loses to the chain), and it fires only once the player has committed: for clause 1 when the costless body 0x021E50DC returns 1, for clause 2 when the cost machine reaches its final phase. Declining therefore burns nothing, and the user confirmed that branch specifically. *** ⚠️⚠️ THE CARD IS NOW DUEL-ONLY, AND THAT IS A REGRESSION FROM CLAUSE 1\'S STATE, accepted by explicit user decision 2026-09-03. Clause 1 alone was two overlay-3 table writes and was puzzle-safe; criteria_row_hook sits inside 0x02243B9C, the row resolver EVERY selecting card passes through, and overlay 41 evicts ov5 in a puzzle -- so a puzzle now crashes on the first selection by ANY card, not merely on this one. *** ⚠️ ONE KNOWN, BOUNDED IMPRECISION: the rider is gated by a ONE-SHOT byte that clause 2\'s resolver sets and the summon-event stub consumes, because opcode 0x14 is a general \'a card arrived on the field\' event and an ungated hook would banish a Jet Synchron summoned any other way. If a clause-2 activation is abandoned after its resolver has run, the byte survives and the next Jet Synchron summon by any means takes the rider.',
             '# the two shared 4-byte hook sites this card depends on, in the STOCK image\nassert h.bytes_at(0x02243BEC, 4, \'ov3\') == bytes.fromhex(\'8449281c\'),                  \'the criteria-row hook site drifted\'\nassert h.bytes_at(0x0224AF96, 4, \'ov3\') == bytes.fromhex(\'00690028\'),                  \'the timing-classifier hook site drifted\'\n# the GY-action registry row this card takes, and its family\nassert h.u32(0x0228E0F8, \'ov3\') == 0x0E64, \'GY-registry row 48 is not the phantom\'\nassert (h.u32(0x0228E0FC, \'ov3\'), h.u32(0x0228E100, \'ov3\'),\n        h.u32(0x0228E104, \'ov3\')) == (0x0E, 0x0224C591, 0x0224C6C1),                  \'GY-registry row 48 is not the Grapha family any more\'\n# the second criteria row\'s donor phantom, and Plaguespreader\'s template row\ncbase, ccount, cstride = 0x022713C4, 0x56C, 12\ncrit = [h.u16(cbase + i * cstride, \'ov3\') for i in range(ccount)]\nassert crit.count(0x0E4A) == 1, \'phantom 0x0E4A no longer owns exactly one row\'\ni = crit.index(0x1EA9)\nassert (h.u16(cbase + i * cstride + 2, \'ov3\'), h.u32(cbase + i * cstride + 4, \'ov3\'),\n        h.u16(cbase + i * cstride + 8, \'ov3\')) == (0xFFFF, 0x0223CB19, 0x000E),                  "Plaguespreader\'s row -- the template for clause 2\'s cost row -- changed"\n# the rider hook site, and the engine\'s own attach it imitates\nassert h.bytes_at(0x02268666, 4, \'ov3\') == bytes.fromhex(\'e089154e\'),                  \'the summon-event default leaf drifted\'\nassert h.bl_target(0x02268662, \'ov3\') == 0x021C479C, \'the shared rider attach moved\'\n# the cost machine we cloned, and the mover we substituted for its own\nassert h.bytes_at(0x021E9038, 4, \'ov3\') == bytes.fromhex(\'feb5051c\'),                  "Plaguespreader\'s cost machine drifted"\nassert h.bl_target(0x021E9120, \'ov3\') == 0x021C6988,                  \'the hand->Deck mover call this clone replaces is no longer there\'\nassert h.bytes_at(0x021C6DB4, 4, \'ov3\') == bytes.fromhex(\'1cb5041c\'),                  \'the hand->GY COST mover drifted\'\n',
             ['notes/jet-synchron-findings.md', 'otn_enhanced/effects/timing_class_hook.py', 'scratch/timing_hook_equiv.py', 'scratch/rowhook_equiv.py'], addr=0x0227900C, oracle='ov3')

    verified('card.jet_warrior_clause_2', 'cards',
             "*** IN-GAME CONFIRMED BY THE USER 2026-09-07, ALL FIVE ORACLES, on ROM sha256 d61470207f26e373240f21ceae5ff304d36385b5d52bb627929d77e6d7113f24 -- their words '1. CONFIRMED / 2. CONFIRMED / 3. Confirmed / 4. Confirmed / 5. Confirmed', reading confirmed by the user before this fact was written. *** JET WARRIOR CLAUSE 2, 'If this card is in your Graveyard: You can Tribute 1 Level 2 or lower monster; Special Summon this card in Defense Position', plus clause 3's two independent once-per-turn latches. THE ORACLES: (1) with NO Level 2 or lower monster on the field the GY effect is NOT OFFERED; (2) with one, the picker lists ONLY Level <= 2, it is tributed, and Jet Warrior arrives in DEFENSE POSITION; (3) using clause 2 does not lock clause 1 in the same turn; (4) declining a prompt does not burn the once-per-turn; (5) clause 1 did not regress. *** THE RIDER ('but banish it when it leaves the field') WAS ADDED AND CONFIRMED SEPARATELY 2026-09-07 on ROM 128e1269...: see rider.summon_rider_hook_is_shared. It is an arm on the shared summon-rider hook, armed by a one-shot byte that ONLY the clause-2 revive sets -- CAVE_JW_C2_POS, which is cid-scoped AND inside the GY self-SS resolver -- so a Synchro Summoned Jet Warrior, which prints no rider, correctly still goes to the Graveyard. *** THE PIECES: a cls2 record at row 643 {0x23EB, 0x0220731D, CAVE_JW_TRIBFILT|1, CAVE_JW_C2_COND|1, CAVE_JW_C2_SLOT4|1, 0} inserted count-neutrally over phantom 0x1655 (the table is BINARY-SEARCHED, so sortedness is mandatory -- verified 0 inversions); a GY-action registry row {0x23EB, 0x0E, 0x0224C591, 0x0224C6C1}; a 4-byte cid-scoped hook at 0x022074E6 for Defense Position; and an arm on the shared timing-class hook. *** THE BUG THAT COST TWO IN-GAME TESTS, AND ITS GENERAL LESSON. Clause 2 was offered, and resolved FOR FREE, on boards with no legal Tribute. The cause was NOT the condition slot: it was that this card's own arm on timing_class_hook -- added for CLAUSE 1 -- substituted the class-2 tag 0x021E51E5 keyed on **cid alone**, and the GY-offer path's `cmp r0,#2 ; beq` at 0x021EDC76 turns class 2 into an UNCONDITIONAL OFFER that never reaches +0C (see dispatch.gy_offer_consults_slot3_and_the_timing_class_can_bypass_it). The fix is one gate, `desc[+5] == 1`, which is STRUCTURAL rather than chosen: 0x0224AF7C reads +0x10 out of the record find_event_handler returns, and find_event_handler picks the table from desc[+5], so class 1 IS 'the classifier is looking at the cls1 record'. *** GENERALISE: A SHARED cid-KEYED HOOK ADDED FOR ONE CLAUSE SILENTLY ANSWERS FOR EVERY OTHER CLAUSE OF THE SAME CARD. Gate every arm on the narrowest field that identifies the clause it was written for -- the Lightpulsar and Jet Synchron arms already did this with a zone/event window, and this arm's 'no window needed' comment was the whole bug. *** AND: the trace that WRONGLY exonerated +0C rested on a BL scan covering ~0xE0 bytes of a 0x290-byte function. Scan whole functions; and when a measurement contradicts a card known to work in game (Grapha), the measurement is the suspect.",
             "from otn_enhanced.cards import jet_warrior as jw\nfrom otn_enhanced.effects import timing_class_hook as tch\nfrom otn_enhanced.effects import ov5_cave\n# the arm exists, and is NOT unconditional any more\narms = {cid: body for cid, _t, body, _d in tch.ARMS}\nassert jw.DONOR_CID in arms, 'Jet Warrior lost its timing-class arm'\nassert 'r4, #0x5' in arms[jw.DONOR_CID], \\\n    'the Jet Warrior arm no longer gates on desc[+5] -- the clause-2 GY offer ' \\\n    'would be unconditionally offered again'\nassert tch.JW_CLS1_CLASS == 1, 'the gated class is not cls1'\n# the stub still assembles, is Thumb-1 only and fits its reservation\nblob = tch.stub(ov5_cave.CAVE_TIMINGHOOK)\nassert len(blob) <= tch.RESERVE, 'the shared timing stub overflowed its reserve'\nfrom otn_enhanced.asm import effect_verify\neffect_verify.assert_thumb1_only(blob, ov5_cave.CAVE_TIMINGHOOK)\n# the engine shapes the fix depends on, against the STOCK image\nassert h.u16(0x021EDC76, 'ov3') == 0x2802, 'the ==2 short-circuit test drifted'\nassert h.u32(0x0224B02C, 'ov3') == tch.TAG_YOU_CAN, 'the class-2 comparand moved'\nassert h.bl_target(0x021EDC8C, 'ov3') == 0x0224AD94, 'the +0C invoker moved'\n# the cls2 table is binary-searched, so our insert must keep it sorted\nkeys = [h.u32(0x02275C04 + i * 0x18, 'ov3') for i in range(0x2B9)]\nassert keys == sorted(keys), 'stock cls2 is unsorted -- the binary search premise'\n",
             ['notes/jet-warrior-findings.md', 'otn_enhanced/effects/timing_class_hook.py', 'otn_enhanced/cards/jet_warrior.py'], addr=0x0227984C, oracle='ov3')

    verified('card.jet_warrior_clauses_0_and_1', 'cards',
             '*** IN-GAME CONFIRMED BY THE USER 2026-09-04, ALL SIX ORACLES, ON THE FIRST TEST. *** Ignition Beast Volcannon 0x23EB -- an EFFECT FUSION MONSTER -- becomes JET WARRIOR (FIRE / Warrior / Synchro / Level 5 / 2100 / 1200), summonable with \'"Jet Synchron" + 1 or more non-Tuner monsters\', with clause 1 (\'If this card is Synchro Summoned: You can target 1 card your opponent controls; return it to the hand\') live. (Clause 2, the GY Tribute revive, and clause 3, the two once-per-turn latches, were not implemented AT THE TIME OF THIS TEST; both are now live and in-game confirmed -- see card.jet_warrior_clause_2.) THE ORACLES: (1) deck editor shows the Synchro frame, Lv5 FIRE Warrior 2100/1200, Extra Deck; (2) Polymerization does NOT offer it and Machine+Pyro no longer fuses into it; (3) it Synchro Summons on Jet Synchron + non-Tuners totalling Level 4; (4) IT REFUSES A DIFFERENT LEVEL 1 TUNER with the same non-Tuners -- the negative control that proves synchro.named_material_table is actually read; (5) QUICKDRAW SYNCHRON works as a substitute Tuner, the free correct ruling from the arm @0x02248636; (6) clause 1 prompts Yes/No, targets 1 CARD (not just monsters) and bounces it. *** PURE DATA -- no injected Thumb, no ov5 slot, no new cls record, no criteria row, no registry row -- so it is PUZZLE-SAFE. *** WHY AN *EFFECT* FUSION DONOR: summon.synchro_trigger_list_has_no_phantom means an \'If this card is Synchro Summoned:\' donor must ALREADY be in 0x0228F6C0, and 0x23EB is row 30. That list\'s 6 Fusion + 3 Ritual members are the ONLY viable donor pool for that timing; an effectless Fusion (the Accel Synchron pool) can carry the chassis but NOT this trigger. Its printed timing already matched (\'When this card is Fusion Summoned: You can target 1 monster your opponent controls\'), so clause 1 is a 20-byte IN-PLACE rewrite of its own cls1[1279] @0x0228D8BC to Nightmare Penguin cls1[325]\'s bounce tuple -- +10 does not move, because both cards print \'You can\'. *** TWO DIFFERENCES FROM carddata.fusion_donor_is_a_synchro_donor\'s effectless case, both measured: card_type 7 -> 37 (not 5 -> 39) and NO genre bit 35, since Jet Warrior is a non-Tuner; and the donor\'s card_genre is NOT the plain {21,29} but {1,10,21,29,34}, because an EFFECT Fusion carries effect-category tags. A whole-table census shows only bits 21/29/36 are class-coupled (147/147, 147/147, 139/140), so the edit is exactly \'clear 29, set 36\' and bits 1/10/34 are LEFT ALONE -- the card inherits Volcannon\'s effect-category tags, a deck-editor-filter cosmetic. Its fusion materials are CATEGORY CODES (7, 4) = \'1 Machine + 1 Pyro\', not cids. *** THE TEST ROM MUST BE A TWO-PATCH BUILD. The material rule is CID-KEYED, so on the clean ROM cid 0x224C is still CHANGER SYNCHRON and the card summons off the wrong Tuner -- it looks like a working test and proves nothing. The first build made this mistake and the user caught it. _build_jet_warrior.py applies the shipped jet_synchron first. GENERALISE: when a card\'s rule NAMES another patched card, the single-card test ROM must contain both.',
             'import struct\nfrom otn_enhanced.cards import jet_warrior as jw\nfrom otn_enhanced.cards import jet_synchron as js\n# the donor, the reference record and the named material\nassert jw.DONOR_CID == 0x23EB and jw.REFERENCE_SYNCHRO_CID == 0x23FE\nassert jw.JET_SYNCHRON_CID == js.DONOR_CID == 0x224C, \\\n    \'the named material is no longer the shipped Jet Synchron donor\'\nassert jw.NEW_CARD_TYPE == 37, \'the target card_type is not Synchro Effect Monster\'\nassert jw.NEW_GENRE == 0x0000001400200402, \'the target genre drifted\'\nassert not (jw.NEW_GENRE >> 35) & 1, \'bit 35 TUNER must NOT be set on a non-Tuner\'\nassert (jw.NEW_GENRE >> 36) & 1 and not (jw.NEW_GENRE >> 29) & 1\n# PART D targets the donor\'s OWN recipe row, material columns only\nassert jw.FUSION_ROW_ADDR == 0x0227106C\nassert h.u16(jw.FUSION_ROW_ADDR, \'ov3\') == jw.DONOR_CID, \\\n    \'fusion row 155 is no longer the donor\'\nassert (jw.FUSION_STOCK_M1, jw.FUSION_STOCK_M2) == (7, 4), \\\n    \'the donor materials are category codes 7/4 (Machine/Pyro), not cids\'\nassert jw.FUSION_DEAD_MATERIAL >= 0x33, \\\n    \'the dead material must be >= 0x33 or it is read as a category code\'\n# the "1 or more" form comes from ABSENCE -- three opt-in exception lists\nassert jw.DONOR_CID not in h.u16_table(0x02275AB8, 16, \'ov3\'), \\\n    \'the donor entered LIST_A, which would break the printed "1 or more" form\'\nassert jw.DONOR_CID not in h.u16_table(0x02275AD8, 21, \'ov3\'), \\\n    \'the donor entered the min-3-materials list\'\nassert jw.DONOR_CID not in jw.TWO_TUNER_CIDS\n# PART E claims the named-material table\'s lone phantom\nassert jw.NAMEDMAT_BASE == 0x02275B04 and jw.NAMEDMAT_COUNT == 23\nassert jw.NAMEDMAT_PHANTOM == 0x2524 and jw.NAMEDMAT_ROW == (0x23EB, 0x224C)\n# PART F rewrites the donor\'s OWN cls1 record, in place\nassert jw.CLS1_ADDR == 0x0228D8BC\nassert h.u32(jw.CLS1_ADDR, \'ov3\') == jw.DONOR_CID, \'cls1[1279] moved\'\nstock = struct.unpack_from(\'<5I\', env.image(\'ov3\'),\n                           jw.CLS1_ADDR - env.base(\'ov3\') + 4)\nassert stock == jw.CLS1_BEFORE, f\'the donor cls1 stock slots drifted: {stock}\'\nassert jw.CLS1_AFTER[3] == jw.CLS1_BEFORE[3] == 0x021E51E5, \\\n    \'slot4 must not move: both cards print the optional "You can"\'\n# ...to Nightmare Penguin\'s tuple, which must still be what we copied\nnp = struct.unpack_from(\'<5I\', env.image(\'ov3\'), 0x02287F4C - env.base(\'ov3\') + 4)\nassert h.u32(0x02287F4C, \'ov3\') == 0x16AB, \'cls1[325] is not Nightmare Penguin\'\nassert np[0] == jw.CLS1_AFTER[0] and np[1] == jw.CLS1_AFTER[1], \\\n    \'the bounce resolver / candidate predicate no longer match the template\'\nassert np[4] == jw.CLS1_AFTER[4], \'the target-declaration thunk no longer matches\'\n# the trigger is INHERITED, not inserted -- and the list has no phantom to spend\ntrig = h.u16_table(0x0228F6C0, 0x24, \'ov3\')\nassert trig[30] == jw.DONOR_CID, \'the donor left the proper-Summon trigger list\'\nassert all(trig[i] < trig[i + 1] for i in range(0x23)), \'trigger list unsorted\'\n',
             ['notes/jet-warrior-findings.md', 'otn_enhanced/cards/jet_warrior.py', '_build_jet_warrior.py'], addr=0x0228D8BC, oracle='ov3')

    verified('card.steam_synchron', 'cards',
             "Cyber-Tech Alligator 0x12B6 -> STEAM SYNCHRON (WATER / Machine / Tuner / Level 3 / 600 / 800): 'During your opponent's Main Phase, you can: Immediately after this effect resolves, Synchro Summon using this card you control (this is a Quick Effect).' Built 2026-09-03 as a pure DATA transplant of Formula Synchron's clause (synchro.opponent_turn_summon_is_formulas_cls3) -- NO injected code and NO ov5 slot, so it is live in every duel mode, puzzles included. FOUR count-neutral edits: cls3 record (drop phantom 0x1528, whose own row is its ONLY binding occurrence anywhere in the ROM), criteria row (drop phantom 0x0E6E), spell-speed-2 list 0x0209C118 (drop phantom 0x1774 -- chosen over 0x0E6B/0x0E6C/0x0E63/0x0E64 because those sit in the T.G. and Infernity set-code tables that other modules assert), and the Synchron set-code list (drop the STALE 0x229E, see archetype.synchron_list_is_full_and_has_a_stale_member). The donor is donor_scan-CLEAN; its one raw ARM9 halfword hit at 0x020A2A84 was chased down and is a coincidence -- that region is a byte ramp read as u16 (the neighbouring 'cids' decode as 1413/1414/1414/1515/1515/1616...). English blobs 20 B name / 182 B desc, so the FULL 152 B official text fits with no paraphrase; j/k/r descs are too small and keep donor text. *** KNOWN DEVIATION, user-accepted before the build: reusing 0x021F1490 verbatim inherits FORMULA'S ONCE-PER-TURN, which the printed card lacks. The condition only READS the turn log; where the stamp happens is NOT proven. Visible only if the player activates and then aborts the material selection. *** IN-GAME CONFIRMED BY THE USER 2026-09-03, ALL EIGHT ORACLES ('Confirmed' x8, then 'ship it!') on rom_steam_synchron.nds sha256 a3bd7debcc4d37020a01a5e7350a06347ade675e7cd67f59cb7e1844fc937268: the Synchro Summon IS offered during the opponent's Main Phase 1 and resolves onto your field on their turn (1); NOT offered on your own turn (2), nor in the opponent's Battle/End Phase (3), nor with no legal Synchro (4); stats and text correct (5); Tuning and Junk Speeder reach it and every other Synchron still does (6, 7); AND IT WORKS IN PUZZLE MODE (8), which is the measured payoff of the data-only build -- an ov5-hosted clause would be inert there. Shipped into apply_all_patches the same day.",
             "import struct\nfrom otn_enhanced.cards import steam_synchron as steam\n# the transplant sources, in the reference (unpatched) images\nassert h.u16(0x0227E1E4, 'ov3') == 0x239E, 'Formula cls3 record moved'\nassert steam.RESOLVER == h.u32(0x0227E1E4 + 4, 'ov3') and \\\n       steam.CONDITION == h.u32(0x0227E1E4 + 0xC, 'ov3'), \\\n    'the module no longer copies Formula\\'s actual slots'\n# the donor is records-free in cls3 and the criteria table\nfor base, cnt, stride in ((0x02279D74, 0x308, 24), (0x022713C4, 0x56C, 12)):\n    hits = [i for i in range(cnt) if h.u16(base + i * stride, 'ov3') == 0x12B6]\n    assert hits == [], f'donor 0x12B6 already owns rows {hits} at {base:#x}'\n# each phantom exists, owns exactly one row in its pool, and has no card_prop\nfor base, cnt, stride, ph in ((0x02279D74, 0x308, 24, steam.CLS3_DROP_PHANTOM),\n                              (0x022713C4, 0x56C, 12, steam.CRIT_DROP_PHANTOM)):\n    hits = [i for i in range(cnt) if h.u16(base + i * stride, 'ov3') == ph]\n    assert len(hits) == 1, f'phantom {ph:#06x} owns {len(hits)} rows at {base:#x}'\n# 0x1528 is the ideal phantom: its own cls3 row is its ONLY occurrence\nimg = env.image('ov3')\nocc = [i for i in range(0, len(img) - 1, 2)\n       if struct.unpack_from('<H', img, i)[0] == 0x1528]\nassert occ == [0x0227A674 - 0x02141700], \\\n    f'0x1528 is no longer occurrence-unique: {[hex(0x02141700 + o) for o in occ]}'\n# the spell-speed and Synchron slots the patch spends\nspd = [h.u16(0x0209C118 + 2 * i, 'arm9') for i in range(0x76)]\nassert steam.QUICKEFFECT_DROP in spd and 0x12B6 not in spd, \\\n    'the spell-speed-2 slot this patch spends is not where it was'\nsyn = [h.u16(0x0209C968 + 2 * i, 'arm9') for i in range(15)]\nassert steam.SYNCHRON_STALE in syn, 'the stale Synchron slot is gone'\n# the moved cls3 window must clear every by-index anchor\nassert max(steam.CLS3_INDEX_ANCHORS) == 527 and 370 in steam.CLS3_INDEX_ANCHORS, \\\n    'the module lost the cls3 by-index anchor list'\n",
             ['notes/steam-synchron-findings.md', 'otn_enhanced/cards/steam_synchron.py', '_build_steam_synchron.py', '_prebuild_steam_synchron.py'], addr=0x0227E1E4, oracle='ov3')

    verified('rider.banish_marker_attach_site', 'continuous_riders',
             "*** WHERE THE 0x1E15 BANISH RIDER IS ATTACHED, AND WHY A DONOR CANNOT GET IT FROM DATA -- the missing half of rider.banish_when_it_leaves_marker, which named 'the per-cid compare chain at 0x02268238' but not its root, its input or its arm. *** THE HOST is the SUMMON-EVENT HANDLER 0x02267A6C, whose r4 is the GLOBAL event record 0x02298A28 (not an argument) and which dispatches on the opcode [r4+0x24] through a jump table at 0x02267AA4. The rider lives under OPCODE 0x14 (0x02267AAC: `cmp r0,#0x14 ; bne ; b 0x02268028`). *** THE PER-CID SWITCH'S ROOT IS 0x022680A8 and its input is `ldrh r2,[r4,#0x12]` -- the summoned card's cid. Its DEFAULT leaf is 0x02268666, the fall-through immediately after the shared attach `0x02268660: movs r3,#3 ; 0x02268662: bl 0x021C479C`. *** THE ARM THAT GRANTS THE RIDER IS 0x02268542 AND IT IS UNGATED: `movs r0,#0 ; str r0,[sp]` (param 0), `ldrh r0,[r4,#0x2]` (side), `ldrh r1,[r4,#0x4]` (slot), `ldr r2,=0x1E15` (the marker key, as an EXPLICIT literal -- which is why Plaguespreader's node carries it too), `b 0x0226846E -> 0x02268660` (kind 3). *** SIMULATED with scratch/summon_event_sim.py (scratch/leave_dispatcher_sim.walk, seeded at r2 rather than r4): Plaguespreader 0x1EA9 AND Quillbolt 0x1E15 BOTH reach 0x02268542 -- the two cards whose measured savestate nodes carry key 0x1E15 -- while Changer Synchron 0x224C, Sword Arm of Dragon 0x0FB1, the records-free Normal Monsters 0x1463 / 0x1F18 and, decisively, TREEBORN FROG 0x19CB (a GY self-Special-Summon that prints NO rider) all take the DEFAULT. The simulator was not told the savestate result; that agreement is the corroboration, the role Deep Diver plays for the leave trees. *** TWO DATA-ONLY ROUTES ARE RULED OUT. The opcode-0x14 prologue runs two membership lists before the switch -- 0x0228F750 (0x2E entries) -> 0x021C479C(side, slot, CID, kind 3, 0) at 0x02268086, and 0x0228F708 (0x24 entries) -> the same with kind 2 at 0x022680A4 -- and BOTH pass the card's own cid as the key. Joining either list gives key 0x224C, while the consumer 0x021B09CC compares against 0x1E15. So the rider needs a CODE hook. *** THE HOOK SITE IS 0x02268666, 4 bytes (`ldrh r0,[r4,#0xe]` 88e0 + `ldr r6,[pc,#0x54]` 4e15, literal 0x022686C0 = 0x000014FC), replaced by a BL that gates on the cid, attaches, REPLAYS BOTH displaced instructions and returns to 0x0226866A (whose `cmp r0,r6` consumes them). r4 must survive; r0 and r6 are both redefined by the replay so they are free; r5/r7 may be live and must be saved; and ⚠️ r6 must NOT appear in the POP list or the pop would undo the replayed literal. *** ⚠️ FIDELITY CAVEAT, UNRESOLVED: opcode 0x14 is a general 'a card arrived on the field' event (five posters: 0x02261542 0x022618E6 0x02265078 0x02265602 0x022656A4, several from sub-type switches) and arm 0x02268542 has no gate, so on the face of it the engine grants Plaguespreader its banish rider on ANY summon, a Normal Summon included. A new card whose printed rider belongs to ONE of its summons should gate the attach on a one-shot byte set by that clause -- CLEARED BY THE STUB, not by the resolver, because the commit 0x0226925C can finish after the resolver returns (the timing window that killed card.upstart_golden_ninja's first STAGE latch).",
             "# the opcode-0x14 door and the switch root's cid load\nassert h.bytes_at(0x02267AAC, 4, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('142800d1'),                  'the opcode 0x14 test drifted'\nassert h.u16(0x022680A8, 'ov3') == 0x8A62,                  '0x022680A8 is not `ldrh r2,[r4,#0x12]` (the switch input)'\n# the shared attach and the default leaf that follows it\nassert h.bytes_at(0x02268660, 4, 'ov3')[:2] == bytes.fromhex('0323'),                  '0x02268660 is not `movs r3,#3`'\nassert h.bl_target(0x02268662, 'ov3') == 0x021C479C, 'the shared attach call moved'\nassert h.bytes_at(0x02268666, 4, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('e089154e'),                  'the default leaf 0x02268666 is not the 4 bytes the hook displaces'\ndef _lit(site):\n    w = h.u16(site, 'ov3')\n    assert w & 0xF800 == 0x4800, f'{site:#010x} is not an LDR literal'\n    return h.u32(((site + 4) & ~3) + (w & 0xFF) * 4, 'ov3')\nassert _lit(0x02268668) == 0x14FC, 'the replayed r6 literal drifted'\n# the rider arm: param 0, then the explicit marker key\nassert h.bytes_at(0x02268542, 4, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('00200090'),                  'the rider arm no longer starts `movs r0,#0 ; str r0,[sp]`'\nassert _lit(0x0226854A) == 0x1E15, 'the rider arm lost its explicit marker key'\n# the two prologue lists really pass the CID as the key, not a marker\nfor site, kind in ((0x02268086, 3), (0x022680A4, 2)):\n    assert h.bl_target(site, 'ov3') == 0x021C479C, f'{site:#010x} is not an attach'\nassert h.u16(0x02268082, 'ov3') == 0x8A62 and h.u16(0x022680A0, 'ov3') == 0x8A62,                  'a prologue list attach no longer passes ldrh r2,[r4,#0x12] (the cid) as the key'\nassert h.bl_target(0x02268074, 'ov3') == 0x02022E14, 'list 0x0228F750 search moved'\nassert h.bl_target(0x02268090, 'ov3') == 0x02022E14, 'list 0x0228F708 search moved'\n",
             ['notes/jet-synchron-findings.md', 'scratch/summon_event_sim.py'], addr=0x02268666, oracle='ov3')

    verified('rider.banish_marker_is_cid_blind_to_the_destination', 'continuous_riders',
             "*** THE 0x1E15 RIDER NODE ALONE MAKES ANY cid BANISH ITSELF ON LEAVING -- the 'WHAT IS NOT YET PROVEN' tail of rider.banish_when_it_leaves_marker, closed STRUCTURALLY 2026-09-03 by reading the consumer chain to its end instead of stopping at the walker query. *** THE PREDICATE IS 0x021B0950(r0 = side, r1 = slot) -> 1 = banish / 0 = graveyard. Disassembled 0x021B0950..0x021B0A1C in full: it queries the family-1 walker 0x021A1430 for marker key 0x20DC, then (after an existence test on the card and a flag test at [0x0229ACD8 + ...] >> 0x15) for 0x1E15 @0x021B09CC, 0x1F5B @0x021B09DE, 0x1F70 @0x021B09F2 and 0x2184 @0x021B0A06, returning 1 on the first hit and 0 at 0x021B0A18 when none is present. *** THE ONLY TWO cid COMPARES IN THE WHOLE FUNCTION ARE EARLY-EXIT ARMS: 0x16F8 and 0x1CE0 @0x021B099A/0x021B09A0, and when they do not match control FALLS THROUGH to exactly the same rider tests. So the four marker keys are tested with NO cid in scope and a donor of any cid reaches them. *** AND THE CALLER TURNS THE 1 INTO THE BANISH. 0x021B0950 has SIX bl callers (0x021B0AFA 0x021CCBDA 0x021CF4B8 0x0222E4A0 0x0222E7DA 0x022621C6; none in arm9). At 0x021CCBDA the register r4 is the DESTINATION ZONE and the sequence is `cmp r4,#0xa ; ble skip ; bl 0x021B0950 ; cmp r0,#0 ; beq skip ; movs r4,#0xf` -- i.e. destination 0x0E (GY) is rewritten to 0x0F (BANISHED), the same encoding card.nast_shipped measured for the destroy-vs-banish switch at 0x021CB490, and the `cmp r4,#0xa` guard means it only applies when the card is actually leaving. The second site 0x021CF4B8 corroborates by suppressing the GY-send bookkeeping (`if (pred) { r4 = 0; r6 = 0; }`). *** CONSEQUENCE: 0x021C479C(side, slot, 0x1E15, 3, 0) is SUFFICIENT; no cid gate stands between the node and the banish. *** AND IT IS NOW IN-GAME CONFIRMED TOO (user, 2026-09-03, card.jet_synchron_clause2): a donor cid that the engine's own per-cid switch never reaches was given this node by an ov5 stub, and the summoned copy was BANISHED rather than sent to the GY when it left the field. So the static chain and the duel agree: the node alone is sufficient for an arbitrary cid.",
             "# the predicate's prologue and the four marker literals it queries\nassert h.bytes_at(0x021B0950, 4, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('70b5324a'), \\\n    '0x021B0950 prologue drifted -- is this still the banish predicate?'\ndef _lit(site):\n    w = h.u16(site, 'ov3')\n    assert w & 0xF800 == 0x4800, f'{site:#010x} is not an LDR literal'\n    return h.u32(((site + 4) & ~3) + (w & 0xFF) * 4, 'ov3')\nassert _lit(0x021B0952) == 0x20DC, 'marker key 1 drifted'\nassert _lit(0x021B09CC) == 0x1E15, 'the banish marker key drifted'\nassert _lit(0x021B09DE) == 0x1F5B, 'marker key 3 drifted'\nassert _lit(0x021B0A06) == 0x2184, 'marker key 4 drifted'\n# every one of them is a family-1 walker query\nfor site in (0x021B0958, 0x021B09D2, 0x021B09E6, 0x021B09FA, 0x021B0A0C):\n    assert h.bl_target(site, 'ov3') == 0x021A1430, f'{site:#010x} is not the walker query'\n# the destination rewrite: cmp r4,#0xa / ble / bl pred / cmp / beq / movs r4,#0xf\nassert h.bl_target(0x021CCBDA, 'ov3') == 0x021B0950, 'the destination-rewrite caller moved'\nassert h.bytes_at(0x021CCBD2, 4, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('0a2c1edd'), \\\n    'the `cmp r4,#0xa ; ble` leaving-guard drifted'\nassert h.u16(0x021CCBE2, 'ov3') == 0x240F, '0x021CCBE2 is not `movs r4,#0xf` (banish)'\nassert h.bl_target(0x021CF4B8, 'ov3') == 0x021B0950, 'the second caller moved'\n",
             ['notes/jet-synchron-findings.md'], addr=0x021B0950, oracle='ov3')

    verified('rider.banish_when_it_leaves_marker', 'continuous_riders',
             "*** 'BUT BANISH IT WHEN IT LEAVES THE FIELD' IS A FAMILY-1 ATTACHED NODE WITH KEY 0x1E15 AND KIND 3 -- MEASURED FROM SAVESTATES 2026-09-02, after TWO static hypotheses were falsified (CLAUDE.md's two-strike rule: this is the measurement, not a third guess). Three states -- Plaguespreader Zombie 0x1EA9 + Quillbolt Hedgehog 0x1E15 in the GY; both Special Summoned from the GY; both banished after being used as Synchro Material -- diffed over the rider pool 0x0229D33C (rider.node_writer_and_kind_byte geometry). BEFORE the summon: no node reachable from any zone chain. AFTER: exactly two nodes, one on each card's OWN zone chain, byte-identical apart from the turn stamp -- {key 0x1E15, kind 3, duration nibble 0, param 0}. After they leave the field both nodes are freed and their pool slots immediately recycled. *** KEY 0x1E15 IS A MARKER CONSTANT, NOT A REFERENCE TO QUILLBOLT -- PLAGUESPREADER'S NODE CARRIES THE SAME KEY. This is the same trap as battle.attacked_this_bp_marker, where key 0x2092 is Ancient Forest's cid used as a marker value because the compiler pools constants by value. *** WHY KIND 3 IS THE RIGHT CLASS: rider.turn_sweeper dispatches kind 3 to 0x0219FA5C, which frees the node ONLY for keys 0x18D9 / 0x1F6A. 0x1E15 is neither, so the node survives every turn sweep -- which is exactly what an open-ended 'when it leaves the field' needs. *** THE PRODUCER IS CID-KEYED, SO A DONOR DOES NOT GET IT FREE: the attach is the queued writer at 0x0226857E (`movs r3,#3 ; bl 0x021C479C`, i.e. 0x021C479C(side, slot, key, kind, [sp+0] = param)) inside the summon path, reached through the per-cid compare chain at 0x02268238. *** THE CONSUMER is 0x021B09CC, `ldr r2,=0x1E15 ; bl 0x021A1430(side, slot, key)` -- the family-1 walker query (kind < 6, node word @+0 compared directly against the key) -- heading a chain that tries further marker keys 0x1F5B, 0x1F70. *** CONSEQUENCE FOR A NEW CARD: do NOT hook the engine's per-cid switch; attach the node yourself with the same call the engine makes, 0x021C479C(side, slot, 0x1E15, 3, param = 0), at Special Summon time. ⚠️ CLOSED 2026-09-03 BY rider.banish_marker_is_cid_blind_to_the_destination: the node ALONE IS SUFFICIENT for an arbitrary cid. This entry used to end 'WHAT IS NOT YET PROVEN: that the node alone makes an arbitrary cid banish itself'; the consumer chain has since been read to its end -- the predicate 0x021B0950 tests the four marker keys with no cid in scope, and its caller 0x021CCBDA rewrites the destination zone 0x0E -> 0x0F on a hit. Still not IN-GAME confirmed.",
             "# the producer: kind 3 through the queued rider writer, in the summon path\nassert h.u16(0x0226857E, 'ov3') == 0x2303, 'the attach no longer passes kind 3'\nassert h.bl_target(0x02268580, 'ov3') == 0x021C479C, 'the attach lost the queued writer'\n# the marker literal, and the two sites that matter\ndef _lit(site):\n    w = h.u16(site, 'ov3')\n    assert w & 0xF800 == 0x4800, f'{site:#010x} is not an LDR literal'\n    return h.u32(((site + 4) & ~3) + (w & 0xFF) * 4, 'ov3')\nassert _lit(0x0226854A) == 0x1E15, 'the producer-side marker literal drifted'\nassert _lit(0x021B09CC) == 0x1E15, 'the consumer-side marker literal drifted'\n# the consumer really is the family-1 walker query\nassert h.bl_target(0x021B09D2, 'ov3') == 0x021A1430, 'the consumer query retargeted'\n# kind 3's sweeper arm frees only two keys, and 0x1E15 is not one of them\nassert 0x1E15 not in (0x18D9, 0x1F6A)\n# both cards that print the rider share the GY self-SS resolver\nB, CNT, STR = 0x02275C04, 0x2B9, 0x18\nrows = {h.u32(B + i * STR, 'ov3'): h.u32(B + i * STR + 4, 'ov3') for i in range(CNT)}\nassert rows[0x1EA9] == 0x0220731D and rows[0x1E15] == 0x0220731D, \\\n    'Plaguespreader / Quillbolt no longer share the GY self-SS resolver'\n",
             ['notes/jet-synchron-findings.md', 'scratch/rider_pool_diff.py'], addr=0x021C479C, oracle='ov3')

    verified('rider.summon_rider_hook_is_shared', 'continuous_riders',
             "*** THE 0x02268666 BANISH-RIDER HOOK IS A SHARED MODULE WITH A cid REGISTER, summon_rider_hook.py, SINCE 2026-09-07 -- AND THE LIFT IS IN-GAME CONFIRMED BY THE USER 2026-09-07, on ROM sha256 128e1269c1f1f3dcff2ce401351e2789db432a9f6228a2373fa252cc069ce441: Jet Warrior revived by its GY effect was BANISHED on leaving, a SYNCHRO SUMMONED Jet Warrior went to the GRAVEYARD (the decisive negative control -- it proves the one-shot byte gates the attach rather than the hook ridering every summon), and JET SYNCHRON DID NOT REGRESS. So the offline equivalence harness and the duel agree. *** The site is a single 4-byte BL, so a stub owned by one card module can only ever serve one card -- the same constraint that produced criteria_row_hook.py and timing_class_hook.py. jet_synchron shipped a private stub at CAVE_JS_RIDER and is in-game confirmed; Jet Warrior needed a second arm, and CAVE_JS_RIDER could not grow because CAVE_JS_ARM sits at exactly CAVE_JS_RIDER + 0x60. So the stub was re-homed to CAVE_RIDERHOOK and the old slot RETIRED -- the CAVE_LP_TIMING -> CAVE_TIMINGHOOK precedent exactly. *** EVERY ARM NEEDS ITS OWN ONE-SHOT BYTE, and the byte is cleared by the CONSUMER, never the setter. Opcode 0x14 is a general 'a card arrived on the field' event with five posters, so an ungated arm would rider a Normal Summon too; and the commit 0x0226925C can finish after the setting resolver returns, which is why the setter must not clear (card.upstart_golden_ninja's first STAGE latch died in that window). *** A NEW ARM MUST FIRST BE SHOWN TO REACH THE DEFAULT LEAF. The attach lives at the DEFAULT leaf of the per-cid switch rooted at 0x022680A8, so a cid with its own dedicated arm NEVER ARRIVES THERE and the hook is silently dead for it. rider.banish_marker_attach_site simulated 0x224C / 0x0FB1 / 0x1463 / 0x1F18 / 0x19CB but NOT the Jet Warrior donor; measured 2026-09-07 with scratch/summon_event_sim.walk: 0x23EB -> 0x02268666 DEFAULT, with the two known-arm controls Plaguespreader 0x1EA9 and Quillbolt 0x1E15 correctly landing on the dedicated arm 0x02268546, which is what validates the walk. *** THE LIFT IS PROVEN TRANSPARENT BY EXECUTION, not by argument: scratch/rider_hook_equiv.py runs the committed pre-lift blob and the shared blob over every (cid x one-shot-byte combination) input and compares FOUR observables -- whether 0x021C479C was called and with which (side, slot, key, kind, param), both one-shot bytes afterwards (so a stub that clears the WRONG card's byte is caught), the replayed r0/r6 that 0x0226866A's `cmp r0,r6` consumes, and that r4 survives. Only the added cid differs. *** JET WARRIOR'S SETTER IS TIGHTER THAN JET SYNCHRON'S: it arms from CAVE_JW_C2_POS, which is cid-scoped AND sits at 0x022074E6 inside the GY self-SS resolver 0x0220731D, four bytes before the commit call -- so only clause 2's revive can arm it and a Synchro Summon of Jet Warrior never does. Jet Synchron arms from its resolver, which leaves the known bounded imprecision that an abandoned activation strands the byte.",
             "from otn_enhanced.effects import summon_rider_hook as rh\nfrom otn_enhanced.effects import ov5_cave\nfrom otn_enhanced.asm import effect_verify\n# the site is still the 4 bytes the shared hook displaces\nassert h.bytes_at(rh.RIDER_SITE, 4, 'ov3') == rh.RIDER_NATIVE,                  'the summon-event default leaf drifted from what the shared hook displaces'\nassert rh.RIDER_SITE == 0x02268666 and rh.RIDER_RESUME == 0x0226866A\n# the node it attaches is the banish marker, family 1\nassert (rh.RIDER_KEY, rh.RIDER_KIND) == (0x1E15, 3), 'the rider node changed'\nassert rh.RIDER_ATTACH & 1, 'the attach constant lost its Thumb bit'\nassert rh.RIDER_ATTACH & ~1 == 0x021C479C, 'the attach target moved'\n# at least two arms, each with a DISTINCT one-shot byte\naddrs = [a for _c, _t, a, _d in rh.ARMS]\nassert len(addrs) == len(set(addrs)), 'two arms share a one-shot byte'\nassert len(rh.ARMS) >= 2, 'the shared module has lost an arm'\n# the emitted stub fits, is Thumb-1 only, and every blx is odd\nblob = rh.stub(ov5_cave.CAVE_RIDERHOOK)\nassert len(blob) <= rh.RESERVE, 'the shared rider stub overflowed its reserve'\neffect_verify.assert_thumb1_only(blob, ov5_cave.CAVE_RIDERHOOK)\n# the retired slot really is retired: nothing may point at it\nassert ov5_cave.CAVE_JS_RIDER != ov5_cave.CAVE_RIDERHOOK\n",
             ['notes/jet-warrior-findings.md', 'scratch/rider_hook_equiv.py', 'otn_enhanced/effects/summon_rider_hook.py'], addr=0x02268666, oracle='ov3')

