    _thumb_fact('engine.mr_cls0_resolver_front_0x0220D530', 0x0220D530, 0x0220D554,
        ['push {r4, lr}', 'adds r4, r0, #0', 'ldrh r1, [r4]', 'ldr r0, [pc, #0x1c]', 'cmp r1, r0', 'bne #0x220d54a', 'adds r0, #0x11',
         'bl #0x21ac204', 'cmp r0, #0', 'ble #0x220d54a', 'movs r0, #0', 'pop {r4, pc}', 'adds r0, r4, #0', 'bl #0x2204724',
         'movs r0, #0', 'pop {r4, pc}'],
        [(0x0220D554, 0x12EA)],
        "0x0220D530(desc) = Monster Reborn 0x12EA's cls0 slot-1 resolver (record 0x0227F5DC +04 = 0x0220D531), 0x28 bytes, decoded from the stock bytes 2026-10-18. "
        "Let cid = u16 desc[0]. If cid == 0x12EA (pool word 0x0220D554) it computes n = 0x021AC204(0x12EA + 0x11 = 0x12FB) (engine.field_cid_count_0x021AC204, "
        "the count of field cards with that cid across both players; cardrows names cid 0x12FB as 'Call of Darkness') and if n > 0 returns 0 WITHOUT doing "
        "anything else. Otherwise (and for any other cid) it calls 0x02204724(desc) and returns 0 in every path (the BL result is discarded: movs r0,#0). "
        "So the resolver itself never reports a result code other than 0. NOT proven: that returning 0 means 'resolution complete' to the caller (phase protocol "
        "not re-derived here), or what 0x12FB does beyond its printed text.",
        "assert h.bl_target(0x0220D53E, 'ov3') == 0x021AC204 and h.bl_target(0x0220D54C, 'ov3') == 0x02204724\n")

