             "engine's restriction surface and not a one-off.\n"
             "*** THE FIVE SITES: (1) 0x021AF176 inside 0x021AF0A8(side, hand slot), the NORMAL "
             "SUMMON predicate (6 callers) -- queries then calls LEVEL_OF_ZONE 0x021B8064 inline. "
             "(2) 0x021BA1F0 inside 0x021BA1E8, a 0x20-byte STANDALONE PREDICATE "
             "0x021BA1E8(r0 = side, r1 = Level) -> 1 allow / 0 deny, the cleanest hook in the "
             "subsystem because the Level ARRIVES AS AN ARGUMENT. (3) 0x021C24FE inside "
             "0x021C2298 -- NOT an enforcement arm: it uses kind filter 2 and POSTS a once-per-turn "
             "marker through the node allocator 0x0219F190. (4) 0x0225D87A inside 0x0225D73C and "
             "(5) 0x0225E0DA -- the two AI PLANNER mirrors, whose deny signal is a local `movs "
             "r7,#0`; site 4 also carries a cid exemption (`ldr r0,=0x1FDB ; cmp r4,r0`).\n"
             "*** THE FEEDER: 0x021BA258(r0 = side, r1 = cid, r2 = ref, r3 = location code) is the "
             "summon-restriction AGGREGATOR with 11 callers -- including 0x021BA69C, the Deck "
             "walker 0x0223BA24 and the hand-SS path 0x0225E51C. It resolves the Level into "
             "[sp+0x8] (LEVEL_OF_CID 0x0202ABD8 for a cid, or 0x021B20AC when the location code is "
             "0xB and a live ref exists, i.e. the CURRENT Level) and passes it to 0x021BA1E8 at "
             "0x021BA368. CONSEQUENCE: hooking 0x021BA1E8 covers the whole Special-Summon surface; "
             "hooking 0x021BA69C (as an earlier plan proposed) would catch only ONE BRANCH of a "
             "tree whose trunk is 0x021BA258.\n"
             "*** WHY THE GATE 0x021B9708 IS THE WRONG PLACE: it is cid-blind on exactly these "
             "paths (summon.legality_gate_and_mode_bits), so a Level condition cannot live there. "
             "*** ANYONE ADDING A NEW LOCK MUST PRESERVE WORM BAIT'S RULE IN THE SAME CODE: these "
             "arms ARE its implementation, so replacing one without re-implementing Level 3-4 "
             "silently unships that card.",
             "# the four pool words that carry Worm Bait's key\n"
             "for p in (0x021AF1C4, 0x021BA208, 0x0225DA0C, 0x0225E2A8):\n"
             "    assert h.u32(p, 'ov3') == 0x2146, f'Worm Bait key pool {p:#x} moved'\n"
             "# (2) the standalone (side, Level) predicate: push/subs #3/cmp #1/bhi, then the query\n"
             "assert h.bytes_at(0x021BA1E8, 8, 'ov3') == bytes.fromhex('08b5c91e012908d8'), \\\n"
             "    '0x021BA1E8 is no longer the Level 3-4 predicate'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021BA1F6, 'ov3') == 0x021A14E8, '0x021BA1E8 lost its node query'\n"
             "# the aggregator feeds it the Level and is the trunk\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021BA368, 'ov3') == 0x021BA1E8, \\\n"
             "    '0x021BA258 no longer calls the Level predicate'\n"
             "# (1) the Normal-Summon arm: node query then LEVEL_OF_ZONE\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021AF17E, 'ov3') == 0x021A14E8, 'Normal arm lost its node query'\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021AF18A, 'ov3') == 0x021B8064, 'Normal arm lost LEVEL_OF_ZONE'\n"
             "# (3) is a WRITER -- it posts through the allocator, it does not deny\n"
             "assert h.bl_target(0x021C252A, 'ov3') == 0x0219F190, \\\n"
             "    'site 0x021C24FE is no longer the marker post'\n"
